('b4f3fdd8-0c9f-4681-9c1d-97625ed57b93', 'Standing Back Stretch', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Standing Back Stretch provides a deep stretch for your back, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '48751201', '48751201-Bodyweight-Standing-Back-Stretch-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Move into the stretch position for Bodyweight Standing Back Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Standing Back Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b522251f-3fce-4cca-b2dd-c1da867377e4', 'Squeeze Bench Press (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Dumbbell Squeeze Bench Press, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '79901201', '79901201-Dumbbell-Squeeze-Bench-Press-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Squeeze Bench Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bench_press', 'Squeeze Bench Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('b526cfd9-5091-4ac0-8f7d-a629e889e544', 'Standing Elbow Circle', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '79821201', '79821201-Standing-Elbow-Circle-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Elbow Circle. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Elbow Circle', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b555d154-4d4d-42dc-9bc9-3a960c776db8', 'Single Straight Leg Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery. A staple exercise that belongs in most training programs.', '43101201', '43101201-Single-Straight--Leg-Stretch-(male)_Pilates.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.079801+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Single Straight Leg Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. Switch sides and repeat for equal time. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Single Straight Leg Stretch', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b559112a-0b54-42e7-9b0b-56e6607a74d1', 'Standing Side Kick', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity kicking exercise that challenges your entire body. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '59611201', '59611201-Standing-Side-Kick-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.870314+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Side Kick. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Side Kick', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b571566f-b457-4c9f-aee2-62e451a98d63', 'Negative Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this crunching movement that works your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '68501201', '68501201-Negative-Crunch-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.52454+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Focus on a slow, controlled lowering phase (3-5 seconds). 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Negative Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b57513ee-20f3-4261-b79b-c41e0f8ea2fc', 'Side Bend (Cable)', 'Core', 'Cables', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Cable Side Bend, focusing on your abs. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '56571201', '56571201-Cable-Side-Bend-(VERSION-2)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Side Bend. 2. Set up in the starting position for Cable Side Bend. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Side Bend', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('b57ddf68-edb7-4c1c-ab08-ee947941c0da', 'Wide Glute Pulse Bridge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this bridging movement focused on hip extension. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '58051201', '58051201-Wide-Glute-Pulse-Bridge-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. At the bottom or top, pulse up and down in small movements before completing the rep. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Wide Glute Pulse Bridge', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b591f0eb-3558-48f7-a74f-cb1dd2dd2af8', 'Ab Roller Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Ab Roller Crunch is a core crunching exercise that primarily targets your abs. The lats, shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '22691201', '22691201-Ab-Roller-Crunch_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.412523+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Ab Roller Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b5923cd7-c838-400f-b167-2157116894f8', 'Standing Top Grab Front Grab', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Top Grab Front Grab is a movement exercise that targets your chest muscles. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '82731201', '82731201-Standing-Top-Grab-Front-Grab-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Top Grab Front Grab. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'core_exercise', 'Standing Top Grab Front Grab', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b5942b9e-fb8b-4199-a250-9c0b36ccea2c', 'Lying Abduction Leg Raise On Floor', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this raising movement that works your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '106841201', '106841201-Lying-Abduction-Leg-Raise-on-floor-(female)_Pilat.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.010404+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Lying Abduction Leg Raise On Floor. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Abduction Leg Raise On Floor. 3. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 4. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Lying Abduction Leg Raise On Floor', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b5986bfa-9cf1-4c37-b05f-648a7baff8b3', 'Standing Gastrocnemius Calf Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build stronger calves with this targeted stretching exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '43191201', '43191201-Standing-Gastrocnemius-Calf-Stretch-(female)_Calves.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.570929+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Gastrocnemius Calf Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your calves. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_stretch', 'Standing Gastrocnemius Calf Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b59b95f7-9dab-40f7-9599-0d29c0c44782', 'Incline Single Arm Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your lateral delts. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '28181201', '28181201-Dumbbell-Incline-One-Arm-Lateral-Raise-(female)_Sh.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Incline Single Arm Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('b59fe3df-e97b-4a31-99b6-94afb2a7d580', 'Right Cross Hook Kick (kickboxing)', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Triceps","Core"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this kicking exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. The shoulders, core assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '88521201', '88521201-Right-Cross-Hook-Kick-(Kickboxing)-(male)_Plyometr.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Right Cross Hook Kick. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Right Cross Hook Kick', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b5a28dc4-0605-4358-ae06-ed146eaa7ba3', 'Side To Front Bend Stretch (Stick)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Stick Side To Front Bend Stretch, focusing on your abs. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '103591201', '103591201-Stick-Side-to-Front-Bend-Stretch-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Stick Side To Front Bend Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Stick Side To Front Bend Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b5a7ef6d-854d-466c-8656-d47a21537673', 'Donkey Kickback (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This kicking exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '44211201', '44211201-Cable-Donkey-Kickback-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Donkey Kickback. 2. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 3. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Donkey Kickback', 'hip_thrust, glute_bridge, leg_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('b5aa4ec0-d07f-45ba-8fef-867387f182e8', 'Assisted Partial Range Inverse Leg Curl', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Assisted Partial Range Inverse Leg Curl targets your hamstrings through a controlled curling motion. Your calves work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '74921201', '74921201-Assisted-Partial-Range-Inverse-Leg-Curl_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 2. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 3. Extend legs back out with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Assisted Partial Range Inverse Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b5ab3605-01ad-45be-8e96-b27a9e641883', 'Mountain Climber Walk', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Mountain Climber Walk builds reactive power and improves conditioning. The hip flexors, shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '47051201', '47051201-Mountain-Climber-Walk_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. From plank position, drive one knee toward your chest. 2. Quickly switch legs, bringing the other knee forward. 3. Continue alternating at a quick pace while maintaining plank form. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your core engaged for stability. Beneficial for overall plyometrics development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'mountain_climber', 'Mountain Climber Walk', 'burpee, plank, high_knees', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b5ad90bc-c963-4355-886f-c24105c3179f', 'Ipsilateral Reverse Lunge (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this lunging movement that develops leg drive and power. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The kettlebell''s offset center of mass increases the stability challenge. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '75821201', '75821201-Kettlebell-Ipsilateral-Reverse-Lunge-(male)_Thighs.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Ipsilateral Reverse Lunge. 2. Step backward, lowering your back knee toward the floor. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Ipsilateral Reverse Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('b5b3b877-e7ef-4510-953f-34ff504b9e81', 'Rowing (Rowing Machine)', 'Back', 'Row Machine', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This cardio exercise keeps your heart rate elevated for improved cardiovascular fitness. Secondary activation of your biceps, rear delts provides additional muscle engagement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight.', '22621201', '22621201-Rowing-(with-rowing-machine)-(female)_Cardio.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Rowing. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'rowing_machine', 'Rowing', 'cycling, running, deadlift', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('b5c11998-2e3d-4bc3-9a62-23af9ce77344', 'Knee Raise Jack', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Knee Raise Jack builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '66761201', '66761201-Knee-Raise-Jack-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Knee Raise Jack. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Knee Raise Jack', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b5c667ad-e59b-40f6-b5df-906747774a26', 'Lying Supine Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Lying Supine Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '36021201', '36021201-Dumbbell-Lying-Supine-Curl-(female)_Forearms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lying Supine Curl. 2. Lie on your back with your body relaxed but ready. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Lying Supine Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('b5cd9989-353a-4fa5-87bc-450c0c71f574', 'Pelvic Tilt', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your abs. Secondary activation of your lower back provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '31481201', '31481201-Pelvic-Tilt-(female)_Hips-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Pelvic Tilt. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Pelvic Tilt', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b5cfcfe7-604f-4c66-b9a7-dd8ba26e660b', 'Hyperextension (Hyperextension Bench)', 'Back', 'Hyperextension Bench', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this extension movement focused on hip extension. Secondary activation of your hamstrings, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '4891201', '04891201-Hyperextension_Hips-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.504261+00', '1. Raise your torso by extending at the lower back/hips. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Hyperextension', 'good_morning, bird_dog, superman', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b5d05d29-17d4-459d-8289-b3e2c7c2fecd', 'Incline Fly (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Dumbbell Incline Fly, an effective flying movement for upper body strength. Secondary activation of your front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '25141201', '25141201-Dumbbell-Incline-Fly-(female)_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Incline Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('b5d30f28-0208-4c6a-827a-79f69b552a2c', '45 Degree Bicycle Twisting Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The 45 Degree Bicycle Twisting Crunch targets your obliques through a crunching motion, building rotational core strength. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '11851201', '11851201-45-degree-Bycicle-Twisting-Crunch_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Bring one knee toward chest while extending the other leg. 2. Rotate to bring opposite elbow toward the bent knee. 3. Alternate sides in a pedaling motion. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'cycling', '45 Degree Bicycle Twisting Crunch', 'crunch, russian_twist, leg_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b5d40962-6dfb-47c6-b79c-a98ef86b368b', 'Seated Military Hold Leg Raise On Floor (Dumbbell) - Alternating', 'Core', 'Dumbbells', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Dumbbell Seated Military Hold Alternate Leg Raise On Floor, focusing on your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '68021201', '68021201-Dumbbell-Seated-Military-Hold-Alternate-Leg-Raise-on-Floor_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.083517+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Seated Military Hold Alternate Leg Raise On Floor. 2. Position yourself on the floor for Dumbbell Seated Military Hold Alternate Leg Raise On Floor. 3. Sit on the floor with your legs positioned as required. 4. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 5. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 6. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. 7. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 64, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Seated Military Hold Leg Raise On Floor - Alternating', 'crunch, plank, v_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', TRUE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('b5f8c1c8-106c-427a-ada2-227d2e921caa', 'Drag Curl (EZ Bar)', 'Arms', 'EZ Bar', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The EZ Barbell Drag Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '59251201', '59251201-EZ-Barbell-Drag-Curl-(VERSION-2)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.422129+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for EZ Barbell Drag Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'EZ Drag Curl', 'EZ Drag Curl', FALSE, 'ez_bar', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('b609e1e1-8de7-4a5c-a4ba-a62ba8c10f8c', 'Side Plank Twist Arm Delt Raise', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'Work your side abdominals with this raising exercise that strengthens your obliques. The shoulders, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '78541201', '78541201-Side-Plank-Twist-Arm-Delt-Raise-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.249384+00', '1. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'side_plank', 'Side Plank Twist Arm Delt Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b60ce03b-7d38-4369-b317-b1c80c5afed9', 'Ring Eccentric Single Leg Curl (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings, Towel', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Strengthen the back of your thighs with this curling exercise. You''ll also feel your calves working to support the movement. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '78721201', '78721201-Ring-Eccentric-Single-Leg-Curl-with-towel_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 2. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 3. Extend legs back out with control. 4. Focus on a slow, controlled lowering phase (3-5 seconds). 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 63, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Ring Eccentric Single Leg Curl With Towel', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('b61f4bef-c4f2-4be0-b135-c9c63cd1bbbd', 'Single Leg Glute Bridge Pullover_back (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell, Flat Bench', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. The kettlebell''s offset center of mass increases the stability challenge. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '35221201', '35221201-Kettlebell-Single-Leg-Glute-Bridge-Pullover_Back_H.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Single Leg Glute Bridge Pullover_back. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Single Leg Glute Bridge Pullover_back', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('b641aefd-6199-4b1c-b723-d76dff87b9c6', 'Squat Jack', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Squat Jack is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic squatting movements. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '75561201', '75561201-Squat-Jack-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Squat Jack', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b642ad44-7ed9-4087-bf0e-0cbf0258712e', 'Prone Press Swan_pilates', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your lats, the Prone Press Swan_pilates helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Secondary activation of your shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '28781201', '28781201-Prone-Press-Swan_Pilates_Pilates.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Lie face down (prone position) for Prone Press Swan_pilates. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Prone Press Swan_pilates, extending through the target muscles. 3. Move into the stretch position for Prone Press Swan_pilates. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Prone Press Swan_pilates', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b644d54d-dcb6-4ef6-b563-2f0c797af869', 'Lying Tuck Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Lying Tuck Crunch, focusing on your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '69341201', '69341201-Lying-Tuck-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Tuck Crunch. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Lying Tuck Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b64b7bff-8c55-41f6-abfc-b34e45608188', 'Assisted Push Up (Resistance Band)', 'Chest', 'Resistance Band', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pushing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '69591201', '69591201-Resistance-Band-Assisted-Push-up-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Assisted Push Up. 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Assisted Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('b64c9c89-42df-4262-b450-f4c9c149029e', 'Split Lunge Stretch (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Split Lunge Stretch is a lunging exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '52351201', '52351201-Dumbbell-Split-Lunge-Stretch_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Split Lunge Stretch. 2. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 72, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Split Lunge Stretch', 'squat, split_squat, step_up, leg_press', TRUE, 'dumbbell', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('b64f6e96-18e4-4625-815c-79a63312b4de', 'Tibialis Anterior Curl (Plate)', 'Legs', 'Weight Plate', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Weighted Plate Tibialis Anterior Curl is a lower body curling exercise that targets your biceps. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '65591201', '65591201-Weighted-Plate-Tibialis-Anterior-Curl-(male)_Calve.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 2. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 3. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Weighted Plate Tibialis Anterior Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'plate', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b656782e-da8b-48c5-a277-3b7eb959d35f', 'Single Leg Tuck Reverse Crunch (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Cable Single Leg Tuck Reverse Crunch is a core crunching exercise that primarily targets your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '79791201', '79791201-Cable-Single-Leg-Tuck-Reverse-Crunch-(female)_Wais.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Single Leg Tuck Reverse Crunch. 2. Lift your hips off the floor by contracting your lower abs. 3. Bring your knees toward your chest, then lower with control. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Single Leg Tuck Reverse Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('b65ce9d3-67f9-4442-ac03-03e5e98e531d', 'Row (Machine)', 'Back', 'Row Machine', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. You''ll also feel your biceps, rear delts working to support the movement. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements. Progress gradually by increasing resistance over time.', '12371201', '12371201-Lever-Row-(plate-loaded)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.452942+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'back_exercise', 'Lever Row', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('b6686f9a-e35e-45b4-9f70-4b923669c36c', 'Jumping Jack', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Calves"}'::text[], 'This cardio exercise keeps your heart rate elevated for improved cardiovascular fitness. Your shoulders, calves work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness. Progress gradually by increasing resistance over time.', '5161201', '05161201-Jumping-Jack-(female)_Cardio.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Jumping Jack. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'jumping_jack', 'Jumping Jack', 'burpee, high_knees, jump_rope', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b67d1481-8f96-43c8-81ae-b9abaf237538', 'Balance Plate Standing', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your lats, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '84751201', '84751201-Balance-Plate-Standing-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Move into the stretch position for Balance Plate Standing. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'balance', 'Balance Plate Standing', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b68caa7e-6340-44f4-ac69-d9be301b8a92', 'Side Step Pulldown', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity pulling exercise that challenges your entire body. Your biceps, upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '98351201', '98351201-Side-Step-Pulldown-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Side Step Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b6967d58-ff30-4db8-b971-88445f0fccbf', 'Chest Out Hands Behind (Hold)', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Chest Out Hands Behind (hold) is a flexibility exercise that targets your chest, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. You''ll also feel your shoulders working to support the movement. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '49451201', '49451201-Chest-Out-Hands-Behind-(Hold)-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Chest Out Hands Behind. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_exercise', 'Chest Out Hands Behind', 'bench_press, chest_fly, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b6a634de-d648-433d-88e1-b0393ab6e38c', 'Pullover To Press (Barbell)', 'Chest', 'Barbell, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Pullover To Press is a pressing exercise that develops back strength and muscle. The lats, triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '221201', '00221201-Barbell-Pullover-To-Press_Back.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Pullover To Press. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Barbell Pullover To Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pullover', 'Pullover To Press', 'bicep_curl, face_pull, lat_pulldown', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('b6b36d72-4eb1-46a8-b7bf-1e883a958aa3', 'Turkish Get Up Squat Style (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. Secondary activation of your shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '5511201', '05511201-Kettlebell-Turkish-Get-Up-(Squat-style)_Thighs.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Turkish Get Up. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'turkish_getup', 'Turkish Get Up', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('b6b3958e-8ad1-47dd-be81-424c9993efb3', 'Lying Twist Toe Touch (Against Wall)', 'Core', 'Wall', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Work your side abdominals with this twisting exercise that strengthens your obliques. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '74411201', '74411201-Lying-Twist-Toe-Touch-against-Wall_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Twist Toe Touch Against Wall. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Lying Twist Toe Touch Against Wall. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'toe_touch', 'Lying Twist Toe Touch Against Wall', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b6baffec-06ab-4e27-a537-f0cc900334b0', 'Double Pulse Squat Kickback', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads","Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This dynamic squatting movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '68921201', '68921201-Double-Pulse-Squat-Kickback-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. At the bottom or top, pulse up and down in small movements before completing the rep. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Double Pulse Squat Kickback', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b6d6c1e0-df23-414b-b360-f300bf5f28a1', '90 To 90 (Stretch)', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your hips, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '65601201', '65601201-90-to-90-Stretch-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for 90 To 90 Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', 'Static / Mobility', 'Static', 'Isolation', 'Bilateral', NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated (Floor)', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', '90 To 90', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b6dd4737-55cb-42cb-9ed2-7a3b390a6e41', 'Lateral Twist Box Jump (Plyo Box)', 'Legs', 'Plyo Box', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings","Calves"}'::text[], 'Enhance your stamina and burn calories with this effective cardio movement. The quads, calves assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight.', '5671201', '05671201-Lateral-Twist-Box-Jump-(female)_Cardio_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Lateral Twist Box Jump. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'box_jump', 'Lateral Twist Box Jump', 'squat, burpee, broad_jump', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b6e3a3e4-11ee-47ed-85c9-b4085c9ec891', 'Leg Downward Dog - Alternating', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Inner Thighs"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. You''ll also feel your hamstrings, calves, shoulders working to support the movement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '49261201', '49261201-Alternating-Leg-Downward-Dog-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Alternating Leg Downward Dog. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Leg Downward Dog - Alternating', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b6efb8c1-e05b-43c6-b224-58d4350c7c09', 'Seated Scapular Adduction', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Seated Scapular Adduction (side Back Pov) is a movement exercise that develops back strength and muscle. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '66141201', '66141201-Sitting-Scapular-Adduction-(side-back-POV)-(female.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Scapular Adduction. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your adductors. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_adduction', 'Seated Scapular Adduction', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b6f2f6bc-ce07-4609-85cf-bd50d03d6992', 'Bird Dog', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back","Glutes"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your glutes, abs provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '31411201', '31411201-Bird-Dog-(female)_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Bird Dog. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bird_dog', 'Bird Dog', 'dead_bug, plank, back_extension', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b6f9ca6d-1b9b-4bcd-bfd0-dee2568c131e', 'Twisted Leg Lunge Pose', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your quads, the Twisted Leg Lunge Pose helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '59061201', '59061201-Twisted-Leg-Lunge-Pose-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Move into the stretch position for Twisted Leg Lunge Pose. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 70, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Twisted Leg Lunge Pose', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b70653e9-1662-4d15-951c-ccdd8f00b8fc', 'Lying Hip Knee Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Lying Hip Knee Raise is a core raising exercise that primarily targets your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '81361201', '81361201-Lying-Hip-Knee-Raise-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Hip Knee Raise. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Lying Hip Knee Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Lying Hip Knee Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b706c25a-bc45-4b4f-8808-2feafa4ecb7c', 'Isometric Mid Thighs Pull', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Isometric Mid Thighs Pull is a pulling exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '96071201', '96071201-Isometric-Mid-Thighs-Pull-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. 2. Set up in the starting position for Isometric Mid Thighs Pull. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your quads. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Isometric Mid Thighs Pull', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b706e25b-07a3-4142-8007-fe410121f69d', 'Single Arm Low Fly (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Dumbbell One Arm Low Fly, an effective flying movement for upper body strength. Your front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '41501201', '41501201-Dumbbell-One-Arm-Low-Fly_Chest.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Single Arm Low Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('b718831c-3ef3-450b-9260-795be9bd33d1', 'Weighted Twisting Crunch (On Bench)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Work your side abdominals with this crunching exercise that strengthens your obliques. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '71201201', '71201201-Weighted-Twisting-Crunch-(on-bench)-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Weighted Twisting Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b71c6609-f367-4c4b-9ce8-6ce996a9aa29', 'Reverse Push Up (TRX)', 'Chest', 'TRX', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Suspender Reverse Push Up is an arm pushing exercise targeting your chest. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '95051201', '95051201-Suspender-Reverse-Push-Up-(male)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.667107+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Reverse Push Up. 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Suspender Reverse Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('b7342315-717f-40ca-b58d-fdcae79e907c', 'Dead Bug', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Dead Bug is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '38001201', '38001201-Dead-Bug-(version-2)-(female)_waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Dead Bug. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dead_bug', 'Dead Bug', 'plank, bird_dog, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b737f858-b4d9-4161-bfae-2d0f6ce8b82d', 'Standing Inside Calf Raise', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Standing Inside Calf Raise isolates your calf muscles through a raising motion. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '105701201', '105701201-Bodyweight-Standing-Inside-Calf-Raise-(male)_Calv.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 3. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 4. Lower with control and repeat. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Standing Inside Calf Raise', 'calf_raise, seated_calf_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b7482fb7-277a-4d3b-bd4a-dc8462e23dd8', 'Single Leg Calf Raise On A Stepbox (Step Platform)', 'Legs', 'Step Platform', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This raising movement focuses on your gastrocnemius and soleus. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength. This variation is excellent for building mind-muscle connection.', '106341201', '106341201-Bodyweight-Single-Leg-Calf-Raise-on-a-Stepbox-(ma.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 3. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 4. Lower with control and repeat. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Single Leg Calf Raise On A Stepbox', 'standing_calf_raise, seated_calf_raise, tibialis_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b75dfb88-86d3-497b-bcb3-00700652e8f5', 'Single Arm Row Rack Support (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell One Arm Row (rack Support) is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '70081201', '70081201-Dumbbell-One-Arm-Row-(rack-support)-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 69, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'dumbbell_row', 'Single Arm Row', 'bent_over_row, lat_pulldown, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('b778e1e5-0a7b-4d00-9760-e86c5f8452ff', 'Seated Circle Leg Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Seated Circle Leg Crunch is a core crunching exercise that primarily targets your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '106831201', '106831201-Seated-Circle-Leg-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.717157+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Seated Circle Leg Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b78c9c39-2d0e-4dcd-9c29-943b98d4871e', 'Narrow Stance Squat (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads","Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Narrow Stance Squat is a rowing exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '56331201', '56331201-Barbell-Narrow-Stance-Squat-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Set up a barbell in a rack at the appropriate height for Barbell Narrow Stance Squat. 2. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Standing', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated)', 'Standard', 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Narrow Stance Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('b78cdb14-b01c-4070-8952-20ea35fe9105', '4 Reverse Lunge Bounce And Kick', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this lunging movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '96361201', '96361201-Bodyweight-4-Reverse-Lunge-Bounce-and-Kick-(female.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Step backward, lowering your back knee toward the floor. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', '4 Reverse Lunge Bounce And Kick', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b79c44da-d872-48cd-a0cb-0ff85a69ffb8', 'Full Squat (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '431201', '00431201-Barbell-Full-Squat_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Set up a barbell in a rack at the appropriate height for Barbell Full Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Full Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('b7a5620c-af8a-4fd1-b73a-cbee0c955ae8', 'Seated Kickback (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This kicking movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '3941201', '03941201-Dumbbell-Seated-Kickback_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Seated Kickback. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 4. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 64, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Seated Kickback', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('b7abe552-8e05-49a6-94aa-3dc260a242e0', 'Weighted Lying Flat Hip Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Weighted Dumbbell Lying Flat Hip Raise, focusing on your core. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '66491201', '66491201-Weighted-Dumbbell-Lying-Flat-Hip-Raise-(female)_Wa.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Weighted Dumbbell Lying Flat Hip Raise. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Weighted Dumbbell Lying Flat Hip Raise. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Weighted Dumbbell Lying Flat Hip Raise. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Weighted Lying Flat Hip Raise', 'Weighted Lying Flat Hip Raise', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('b7c699e2-11a2-40a6-b76d-61469a986d33', 'Pronate Grip Triceps Extension (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This extension movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '3731201', '03731201-Dumbbell-Pronate-grip-Triceps-Extension_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Pronate Grip Triceps Extension. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Pronate Grip Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('b7dcf29d-e423-4a5a-b45c-73cc82fc8fa8', 'Hang Clean And Press (Dumbbell)', 'Full Body', 'Dumbbells', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Quads","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Hang Clean And Press is a compound pressing exercise that engages your entire body. You''ll also feel your shoulders, legs working to support the movement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '83371201', '83371201-Dumbbell-Hang-Clean-and-Press-(male)_Weightlifting.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.123147+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Hang Clean And Press. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Dumbbell Hang Clean And Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'clean', 'Hang Clean And Press', 'power_clean, clean, front_squat', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('b7ee6d81-2674-4e60-95c5-bd7820bb476a', 'Lying Single Leg Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '66831201', '66831201-Lying-Single-Leg-Raise-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Single Leg Raise. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Lying Single Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b7f64fde-a13f-4e6c-a398-93bf2844129d', 'Cross Over Reverse Fly (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Cable Cross Over Reverse Fly, an effective shoulder flying exercise. Your upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '24921201', '24921201-Cable-Cross-over-Revers-Fly-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.723232+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Cross Over Reverse Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Cross Over Reverse Fly', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, push_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('b805925f-7764-42bc-bdaa-c91406525a9a', 'Cow Yoga Pose Bitilasana', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Cow Yoga Pose Bitilasana provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '69011201', '69011201-Cow-Yoga-Pose-Bitilasana-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Cow Yoga Pose Bitilasana. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Cow Yoga Pose Bitilasana', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b80ec9c5-cfc1-4df7-b43f-ef3ed648f87f', 'Push Up (Plate)', 'Chest', 'Weight Plate', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Weighted Plate Push Up, an effective pushing movement for upper body strength. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '80761201', '80761201-Weighted-Plate-Push-up-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.242428+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set. A solid choice for chest day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Weighted Plate Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'plate', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b817a281-2e9a-4c73-bb6f-237ea0b02e3c', 'Standing Straight Arm Chest Fly', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This flying exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. The front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '73651201', '73651201-Bodyweight-Standing-Straight-Arm-Chest-Fly-(male)_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Standing Straight Arm Chest Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b820e30f-6b57-4049-9351-d6f307cfbfbb', 'Seated Hamstring Stretch (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings, Chair', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This stretching movement works your hamstrings for balanced leg development. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '73101201', '73101201-Seated-Hamstring-Stretch-with-Chair-(female)_Thigh.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.717157+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction. Works well for hamstrings activation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hamstring_stretch', 'Seated Hamstring Stretch With Chair', 'stretch_hip, stretch_calf, stretch_back', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('b821793f-4cf8-47a4-ae27-e8da72eff9d2', 'Lying Rear Decline Bridge', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Rear Decline Bridge, focusing on your abs. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The decline position targets the lower portion of the muscles more intensely. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '6681201', '06681201-Rear-Decline-Bridge_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.483269+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', 'Bridge', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 53, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Rear Decline Bridge', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b822dab4-1436-4b42-9cc4-9cf32cbb7648', 'Back Kick Heel Touches', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Back Kick Heel Touches is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic kicking movements. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '60901201', '60901201-Back-Kick-Heel-Touches-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Back Kick Heel Touches. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Back Kick Heel Touches', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b84fbfb2-ce44-4799-b986-69dcfc08c20c', 'Standing Swimmer', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Standing Swimmer is a movement exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '49401201', '49401201-Standing-Swimmer-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Swimmer. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'swimming', 'Standing Swimmer', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b8516199-c0ec-4301-a13a-9050201ffc86', 'Seated Single Leg Tibialis Press', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Seated Single Leg Tibialis Press isolates your calf muscles through a pressing motion. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '105351201', '105351201-Seated-Single-Leg-Tibialis-Press-(male)_Calves-FI.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Seated Single Leg Tibialis Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 67, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Seated Single Leg Tibialis Press', 'squat, leg_extension, leg_curl, hack_squat, lunge', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b864ed5b-da95-4bfa-b7a0-f1dc49d00233', 'Knee Drive To Leg Lift', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Knee Drive To Leg Lift builds reactive power and improves conditioning. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '75761201', '75761201-Knee-Drive-to-Leg-Lift-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Knee Drive To Leg Lift. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'Knee Drive To Leg Lift', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b884bb55-9837-4b81-b1a7-031d6244aae6', 'Push Up (with Push Up Handles)', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pushing movement that develops pressing power. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement.', '14861201', '14861201-Push-up-(With-push-up-handles)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. Great for building strength in your chest.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b884d16a-c7e3-43c6-bb82-f2e9b12a60b5', 'Front Plank Butt', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Front Plank Butt is a core stabilization exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your shoulders, lower back working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '23471201', '23471201-Front-Plank---Butt-(WRONG-RIGHT)_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Front Plank Butt', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b889b1af-cab3-429c-8b97-466bb64236c4', 'Straight Leg Glute Bridge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this bridging movement that emphasizes the glutes. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '74191201', '74191201-Straight-Leg-Glute-Bridge-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.340041+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout. This variation specifically emphasizes the glutes.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Straight Leg Glute Bridge', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b88fbc68-0fb2-4f73-9997-32d032313a34', 'Kneeling High To Low Fly (Cable)', 'Chest', 'Cables', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This flying exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. You''ll also feel your front delts working to support the movement. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '65421201', '65421201-Cable-Kneeling-High-to-Low-Fly-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Set the cable pulley to the highest position and attach your preferred handle. 2. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 3. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 4. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 5. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Kneeling High To Low Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('b89f1df0-e85d-4a43-a38b-08d6db5abc0b', 'Lying Single Leg Squat (Sled)', 'Legs', 'Sled', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Sled Lying Single Leg Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '107641201', '107641201-Sled-Lying-Single-Leg-Squat_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.737494+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Sled Lying Single Leg Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pistol_squat', 'Sled Lying Single Leg Squat', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b89fd252-9658-409c-94aa-f098d7cda083', 'Isometric Hold Wide Hand Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pushing movement that develops pressing power. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts. This is a great exercise for all fitness levels with proper scaling.', '93111201', '93111201-Isometric-Hold-Wide-Hand-Push-up-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control. Works well for chest activation.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Isometric Hold Wide Hand Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b8a02168-65e0-477a-8668-43204227f26d', 'Incline Bench Press (Smith Machine)', 'Chest', 'Smith Machine, Flat Bench', '{Pectorals}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '70031201', '70031201-Smith-Incline-Bench-Press-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Incline Bench Press. 2. Set the bench to an incline angle (30-45 degrees). 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 96, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'incline_press', 'Smith Incline Bench Press', 'Incline Bench Press', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('b8a4d73a-4e11-4d67-add7-fb20104e89af', 'Step Jack Punch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic stepping movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '69301201', '69301201-Step-Jack-Punch-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Step Jack Punch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Step Jack Punch', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b8b5917f-b8ce-4f73-9305-379c6f10086e', 'Single Leg Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts. A staple exercise that belongs in most training programs.', '75601201', '75601201-Bodyweight-Single-Leg-Squat-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.667107+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pistol_squat', 'Single Leg Squat', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b8b697c6-6ee3-4d5b-8c62-67f57e7ffdf2', 'Sumo Quarter Squat Tip Toe - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic squatting movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. Excellent for pre-exhausting the target muscle before compound lifts.', '53241201', '53241201-Sumo-Quarter-Squat-Alternate-Tip-Toe-(female)_Plyo.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.340041+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Sumo Quarter Squat Tip Toe - Alternating', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b8ced0dd-2118-45d5-bf0d-0bf2f795d36a', 'Side Step Rainbow Arms', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity stepping exercise that challenges your entire body. The quads assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '97811201', '97811201-Side-Step-Rainbow-Arms-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Step Rainbow Arms. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Side Step Rainbow Arms', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b8d5ff26-ec6d-45dc-92bb-81cc83e680f7', 'Seated Toe Touch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '76981201', '76981201-Sitting-Toe-Touch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Toe Touch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'toe_touch', 'Seated Toe Touch', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b8d961bf-0430-4052-ab7f-8685363a5fea', 'Single Leg Deadlift With Arm And Leg Extended', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings","Traps"}'::text[], 'The Single Leg Bodyweight Deadlift With Arm And Leg Extended is a lower body hip hinge exercise that targets your hamstrings/glutes. The glutes, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '29201201', '29201201-Single-Leg-Bodyweight-Deadlift-with-Arm-and-Leg-Extended-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 2. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 3. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'deadlift', 'Single Leg Deadlift With Arm And Leg Extended', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust, leg_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b8e8d2d8-0fc2-4306-835f-ba4c4cdeb053', 'Hip Thrust (Smith Machine)', 'Legs', 'Smith Machine', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Core"}'::text[], 'The Smith Hip Thrust is a hip-dominant thrusting exercise that targets your glutes. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '57611201', '57611201-Smith-Hip-Thrust-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Hip Thrust. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_thrust', 'Smith Hip Thrust', 'Hip Thrust', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('b91e825f-0a75-44fe-9055-ce94d64b548f', 'Cross Body Elbow To Knee Side To Side Hop', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'The Cross Body Elbow To Knee Side To Side Hop is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. You''ll also feel your shoulders, core working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '105181201', '105181201-Cross-Body-Elbow-to-Knee-Side-to-Side-Hop-(male)_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.504261+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Cross Body Elbow To Knee Side To Side Hop. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_stretch', 'Cross Body Elbow To Knee Side To Side Hop', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b934a405-83eb-4c81-affe-e8d48ca862c2', 'Bent Leg Kickback Kneeling (Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Bent Leg Kickback (kneeling) is a hip-dominant kicking exercise that targets your glutes. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '21491201', '21491201-Resistance-Band-Bent-Leg-Kickback-(Kneeling)-(fema.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Bent Leg Kickback. 2. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 3. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 4. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 47, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Bent Leg Kickback', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('b938998f-8f87-4da3-9fc8-976295f69d56', 'Lying Flat Hip Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this raising movement that works your abs. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '73781201', '73781201-Lying-Flat-Hip-Raise-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.249384+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Flat Hip Raise. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Lying Flat Hip Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Lying Flat Hip Raise', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b93d23cc-4375-403e-bd42-7160a4ea997d', 'Standing Pelvic Tilt (Against Wall)', 'Core', 'Wall', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your core. The standing position engages your core for stability. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '79431201', '79431201-Standing-Pelvic-Tilt-against-Wall-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.870314+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 44, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Pelvic Tilt Against Wall', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b945528a-ac73-4e6e-a1fd-ba70aa477449', 'Walking On Spot', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this stepping exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '90531201', '90531201-Walking-On-Spot-(VERSION-2)-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Walking On Spot. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Walking On Spot', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b9455baa-f4ae-4de3-96a3-38a7464c1567', 'Straight Arm Twisting Sit Up (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Straight Arm Twisting Sit Up targets your obliques through a twisting motion, building rotational core strength. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '42511201', '42511201-Dumbbell-Straight-Arm-Twisting-Sit-up_Waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Straight Arm Twisting Sit Up. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Dumbbell Straight Arm Twisting Sit Up. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 74, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Straight Arm Twisting Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('b9492726-f07f-41bf-a4cd-f8d89333a839', 'Finger Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '14371201', '14371201-Dumbbell-Finger-Curls_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Finger Curls. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Finger Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('b95d5063-46e5-40a3-bbd9-aee5e3ea3df7', 'Lying Hip Circle', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Lying Hip Circle is a lower body movement exercise that targets your delts. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '67041201', '67041201-Lying-Hip-Circle-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Hip Circle. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Hip Circle. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_circle', 'Lying Hip Circle', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b968d843-a167-45e4-a7d7-564099b872aa', 'Arms Circle Front Step', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Arms Circle Front Step is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic stepping movements. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '57131201', '57131201-Arms-Circle-Front-Step-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Arms Circle Front Step. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Arms Circle Front Step', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b9692a94-6770-451a-89c8-fb87d6296d40', 'Lying Butterfly Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this flying movement that works your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '77351201', '77351201-Lying-Butterfly-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Butterfly Crunch. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'groin_stretch', 'Lying Butterfly Crunch', 'plank, leg_raise, russian_twist, sit_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b975c55b-ee44-4447-8ac0-366072aa0323', 'Seated Shoulder Press (Chair)', 'Shoulders', 'Chair', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Seated Shoulder Press On A Chair, an effective shoulder pressing exercise. Secondary activation of your triceps provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '86331201', '86331201-Seated-Shoulder-Press-on-a-Chair-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form. This exercise is excellent for delts development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 67, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Seated Shoulder Press On A Chair', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b986e88c-513a-479a-9a59-db59815b3cca', 'Reverse Calf Raise (Smith Machine)', 'Legs', 'Smith Machine', '{Tibialis Anterior}'::text[], '{Calves}'::text[], 'The Smith Reverse Calf Raises isolates your calf muscles through a raising motion. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '7631201', '07631201-Smith-Reverse-Calf-Raises_Calves_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Reverse Calf Raises. 2. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 3. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 4. Lower with control and repeat. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Smith Reverse Calf Raise', 'Reverse Calf Raises', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('b98bbabb-0a86-445a-ac03-e04ef07c62f9', 'High Row - Overhand Grip (Band)', 'Back', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. Your biceps, rear delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '70461201', '70461201-Band-Narrow-Grip-High-Row-(VERSION-2)-(female)_Bac.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Narrow Grip High Row. 2. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'close_grip_bench', 'High Row - Narrow Grip', 'High Row - Narrow Grip', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('b98c6338-7e38-4448-8d52-7a86d09454c2', 'Assisted Parallel Pull Up - Close Grip (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Assisted Parallel Close Grip Pull Up is a pulling exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. The biceps, upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '97561201', '97561201-Assisted-Parallel-Close-Grip-Pull-up-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 2. Pull yourself up by driving your elbows down and back. 3. Continue until your chin clears the bar, then lower with control to a full hang. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Assisted Parallel Pull Up - Close Grip', 'Assisted Parallel Pull Up - Close Grip', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b99b1ee4-672a-46a4-9582-ac7f7d80234d', 'Single Arm Pull Up (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Single Arm Pull Up is a pulling exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. You''ll also feel your biceps, upper back working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '69621201', '69621201-Single-Arm-Pull-up-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Pull yourself up by driving your elbows down and back. 2. Continue until your chin clears the bar, then lower with control to a full hang. 3. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Single Arm Pull Up', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b9b2e0a6-e6cd-4e6c-9eb3-e2ed07533546', 'Donkey Kick Glute Curl', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this curling movement that emphasizes the glutes. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '65681201', '65681201-Donkey-Kick-Glute-Curl-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 2. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 3. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set. A solid choice for legs day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Donkey Kick Glute Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b9b9dae0-17f6-40b6-bb01-db239710b4ff', 'Criss Cross Jack', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Criss Cross Jack is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '49991201', '49991201-Criss-Cross-Jack-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Criss Cross Jack. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Criss Cross Jack', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b9c19f39-b3c8-4a0e-99e6-cf590d405a9c', 'Mixed Grip Deadlift (Barbell)', 'Back', 'Barbell', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings","Traps"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Mixed Grip Deadlift is a lower body hip hinge exercise that targets your hamstrings/glutes. You''ll also feel your glutes, lower back working to support the movement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '72361201', '72361201-Barbell-Mixed-grip-Deadlift-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.937212+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Mixed Grip Deadlift. 2. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 3. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 4. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'deadlift', 'Mixed Grip Deadlift', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust, leg_curl', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('b9c1d197-7dc0-46a6-bcc1-825d81b3088a', 'Single Leg Calf Jump', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Single Leg Calf Jump is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic jumping movements. The quads, calves assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '107541201', '107541201-Single-Leg-Calf-Jump-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 2. Set up in the starting position for Single Leg Calf Jump. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 45, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Single Leg Calf Jump', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b9c1fe68-68e0-4e54-9db6-3385e4e3f340', 'Wide Child Prasarita Balasana Yoga Pose', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Wide Child Prasarita Balasana Yoga Pose is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '78371201', '78371201-Wide-Child-Prasarita-Balasana-Yoga-Pose-(female)_S.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Wide Child Prasarita Balasana Yoga Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Wide Child Prasarita Balasana Yoga Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b9c5fdf6-0879-4a90-afa1-b0f344190a91', 'Wall Plank (Wall)', 'Core', 'Wall', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this stabilization movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your shoulders, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '73891201', '73891201-Wall-Plank-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.384461+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 3. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 4. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Wall Plank', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b9cfa548-e856-4dae-8fdb-91ba54eaaade', 'Sit (Against Wall)', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This movement movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '66961201', '66961201-Sit-(wall)-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.628647+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Set up in the starting position for Sit. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your quads. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Sit', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b9db4c01-f29a-4f42-8623-6f687c0e0415', 'Standing Curl - Wide Grip (Barbell)', 'Arms', 'Barbell', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. The standing position engages your core for stability. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '1131201', '01131201-Barbell-Standing-Wide-grip-Curl_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Standing Wide Grip Curl. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Standing Curl - Wide Grip', 'Standing Curl - Wide Grip', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('b9dee38b-dcec-42d3-966e-23f45fce5ed7', 'Bench Dip Knees Bent (Flat Bench)', 'Chest', 'Flat Bench', '{"Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Bench Dip (knees Bent) targets your triceps through a dipping motion. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '1291201', '01291201-Bench-Dip-(knees-bent)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 2. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Bench Dip', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('b9e66551-8a78-40fb-a6c5-a8b965a6f25a', 'Leg Press (Smith Machine)', 'Legs', 'Smith Machine', '{Quadriceps}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this pressing exercise for quad development. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '7601201', '07601201-Smith-Leg-Press_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Leg Press. 2. Position your feet on the platform and release the safety. 3. Lower the weight by bending your knees, then press back up powerfully. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'leg_press', 'Smith Leg Press', 'Leg Press', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('b9f113a5-e934-4b19-b29d-d437c7323f67', 'Roll Neck Rotation Lying On Floor', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your neck with this rotation exercise for improved stability. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Include this exercise in your routine for balanced strength development.', '54101201', '54101201-Roll-Neck-Rotation-Lying-on-Floor-(female)_Neck_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Roll Neck Rotation Lying On Floor. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Roll Neck Rotation Lying On Floor. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Roll Neck Rotation Lying On Floor. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'neck_stretch', 'Roll Neck Rotation Lying On Floor', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ba02c30f-0c64-40c6-92bd-19a093121eb0', 'Single Arm Fly (Resistance Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Single Arm Fly is a flying exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. The front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '91281201', '91281201-Resistance-Band-Single-Arm-Fly-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.128549+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Single Arm Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Single Arm Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('ba055f1c-6c8a-4f92-bd92-4379f17c671c', 'Incline Shoulder Press With V Bar - Close Grip (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Shoulders","Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Cable Incline Close Grip Shoulder Press With V Bar, an effective shoulder pressing exercise. The triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '86621201', '86621201-Cable-Incline-Close-Grip-Shoulder-Press-with-V-Bar.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.737494+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Incline Close Grip Shoulder Press With V Bar. 2. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 83, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Incline Shoulder Press With V Bar - Close Grip', 'Incline Shoulder Press With V Bar - Close Grip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('ba12b46e-e5bb-4d57-994c-a275bc651113', 'Stability Ball Seated Balance Knee Extension (Stability Ball)', 'Legs', 'Stability Ball', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this extension movement that develops leg drive and power. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Using a ball requires constant core engagement to maintain balance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '100211201', '100211201-Stability-Ball-Sitting-Balance-Knee-Extension-(fe.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Stability Ball Seated Balance Knee Extension. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Extend through the target joint(s) for Stability Ball Seated Balance Knee Extension. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_extension', 'Stability Ball Seated Balance Knee Extension', 'squat, leg_press, lunge', FALSE, 'stability_ball', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ba2784b3-49f1-49a7-b282-8e39e189bb8a', 'Side Step Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '63171201', '63171201-Side-Step-Squat-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Side Step Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ba36889a-ae66-4640-9e3a-6df41c1864ac', 'Shrug (Band)', 'Back', 'Resistance Band', '{"Traps"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this shrugging movement targeting your traps. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '10181201', '10181201-Band-shrug_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.247914+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Shrug. 2. Shrug your shoulders straight up toward your ears. 3. Hold briefly at the top, then lower with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shrug', 'Shrug', 'deadlift, bent_over_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('ba39bfc8-1c6d-46ac-8f89-d776cffd36a6', 'Leg Raise With Head Up - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this raising movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '74501201', '74501201-Alternate-Leg-Raise-with-Head-up-(VERSION-2)_Waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 2. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 3. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, 'Static', 'Compound', 'Bilateral (Alternating)', NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Leg Raise With Head Up - Alternating', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ba405f78-c347-4ea6-a09e-6ab817d53daa', 'Back Slaps Wrap Arround Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your back, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '88431201', '88431201-Back-Slaps-Wrap-Arround-Stretch-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Back Slaps Wrap Arround Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Back Slaps Wrap Arround Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ba567a26-27ed-46d1-acd6-172559f7396d', 'Diamond Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this pushing exercise for bigger arms. Secondary activation of your chest provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '26971201', '26971201-Diamond-Push-up-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled. Ideal for triceps strength and endurance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Diamond Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ba597438-a2c9-4c2b-82c1-8495f2c95cfd', 'Child Pose Arms Rotation', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your back, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Secondary activation of your hips provides additional muscle engagement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '77621201', '77621201-Child-pose-Arms-Rotation-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Child Pose Arms Rotation. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Move into the stretch position for Child Pose Arms Rotation. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Child Pose Arms Rotation', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ba714377-5694-4ded-a398-65117f945722', 'Head Supported Row (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Head Supported Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '47411201', '47411201-Dumbbell-Head-Supported-Row_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Head Supported Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'general_exercise', 'Head Supported Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ba738955-cc5e-42b8-a2b2-bedeba70399a', 'Seated Shoulder 90 Degrees Internal Rotation', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Seated Shoulder 90 Degrees Internal Rotation is a rotation exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '55021201', '55021201-Seated-Shoulder-90-degrees-Internal-Rotation_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.083517+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Seated Shoulder 90 Degrees Internal Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Seated Shoulder 90 Degrees Internal Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ba7e0f87-39bf-4a65-98b3-59a98226ea88', 'Butterfly Forward Leaning', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your adductors, the Butterfly Forward Leaning helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. You''ll also feel your hips working to support the movement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '96641201', '96641201-Butterfly-Forward-Leaning-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.079801+00', '1. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 2. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 3. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'groin_stretch', 'Butterfly Forward Leaning', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('ba8b5687-ca8a-4074-b958-c6ff6ec036a0', 'Half Kneeling Face Pull (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'The Cable Half Kneeling Face Pull is a pulling exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. You''ll also feel your upper back, rotator cuff working to support the movement. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '77431201', '77431201-Cable-Half-Kneeling-Face-Pull_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Half Kneeling Face Pull. 2. Get into a half-kneeling position (one knee down, opposite foot forward). 3. Pull the rope toward your face, separating your hands as you pull. 4. Squeeze your rear delts and upper back at peak contraction. 5. Return with control, maintaining cable tension. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'face_pull', 'Half Kneeling Face Pull', 'rear_delt_fly, bent_over_row, lateral_raise', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('ba93cc98-be09-4bca-ac7b-f91349e84b90', 'Standing Calf Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build stronger calves with this targeted raising exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '4171201', '04171201-Dumbbell-Standing-Calf-Raise_Calves-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Calf Raise. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 4. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 5. Lower with control and repeat. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 94, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Standing Calf Raise', 'calf_raise, seated_calf_raise', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('ba9e28d0-85d0-4845-a635-696eafa13ec3', 'Arms Up And Down', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '87471201', '87471201-Arms-Up-and-Down-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Arms Up And Down. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Arms Up And Down', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('baa26528-a978-4ef9-80c6-958ea1d0c314', 'Back And Shoulders Stretch', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your back, the Back And Shoulders Stretch helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '53671201', '53671201-Back-and-Shoulders-Stretch-(female)_Back-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Back And Shoulders Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Back And Shoulders Stretch', 'stretch_chest, stretch_tricep, stretch_lat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('baa5da7b-016e-46a3-9c54-72fbbbaf47ca', 'Side Lying Clam And Kick', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this kicking movement focusing on your glute med/abductors. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '58711201', '58711201-Side-Lying-Clam-and-Kick-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Lying Clam And Kick. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glute med/abductors. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Side Lying Clam And Kick', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('baa615a1-be95-46d8-89c2-127f867665b5', 'Shoulder Flexion', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this flexion movement focusing on your delts. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '106901201', '106901201-Shoulder---Flexion-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Shoulder Flexion. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Shoulder Flexion', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bab856fd-fe12-459b-ae25-aa0713206610', 'Far Leg Hip Thrust', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Core"}'::text[], 'This thrusting exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '65731201', '65731201-Far-Leg-Hip-Thrust-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.505723+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_thrust', 'Far Leg Hip Thrust', 'glute_bridge, romanian_deadlift, leg_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('babbac05-985c-483f-89c4-a0546690f9fa', 'Dynamic Back Stretch', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Dynamic Back Stretch provides a deep stretch for your back, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '46711201', '46711201-Dynamic-Back-Stretch-(male)_Back.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Dynamic Back Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Dynamic Back Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('babfaecd-fe4a-4fe5-a4a0-d5928f5e4ee3', 'Seated Leg Curl (Plate Loaded Machine)', 'Legs', 'Leg Curl Machine', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This curling movement works your hamstrings for balanced leg development. The calves assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '86041201', '86041201-Lever-Seated-Leg-Curl-(plate-loaded)-(male)_Thighs.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.271124+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Leg Curl. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 4. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 5. Extend legs back out with control. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Lever Seated Leg Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('bac56005-2540-423b-9a90-a5babf12a77d', 'Tabletop Plank Raise And Reach', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this raising movement that works your abs. You''ll also feel your shoulders, lower back working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '78321201', '78321201-Tabletop-Plank-Raise-and-Reach-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Tabletop Plank Raise And Reach. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Tabletop Plank Raise And Reach', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bae30d89-6dbb-4db2-9b22-543934a95c7f', 'Hip Swirls', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this movement movement focused on hip extension. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '51141201', '51141201-Hip-Swirls-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Hip Swirls. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Hip Swirls', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bb0550df-e760-4052-b948-a30a23679b08', 'Snatch Pull', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Develop functional strength with the Snatch Pull, a comprehensive pulling exercise. The quads, shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '7761201', '07761201-Snatch-Pull_Weightlifting_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.689343+00', '1. Explosively pull the weight from the floor/hang position. 2. As it rises, pull yourself under and catch it overhead with locked arms. 3. Stand to complete the lift. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'snatch', 'Snatch Pull', 'power_snatch, clean, overhead_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bb05ec3c-45d7-4f7c-a8c7-802620bbfcf0', 'Seated Hip Flexion (Resistance Band)', 'Core', 'Resistance Band', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Seated Hip Flexion is a lower body flexion exercise that targets your core. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '101491201', '101491201-Resistance-Band-Seated-Hip-Flexion-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.128549+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Seated Hip Flexion. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Seated Hip Flexion', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('bb10eed9-689c-45a5-8ca0-50e5223630d7', 'Squat Leg Side Lift', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic squatting movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '74881201', '74881201-Squat-Leg-Side-Lift-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears. An effective movement for your plyometrics routine.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Squat Leg Side Lift', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bb120804-dfaf-4247-8bd1-af0b13e8d1f8', 'Upavishta Konasana Yoga Pose', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your full body area and enhance overall flexibility. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '79741201', '79741201-Upavishta-Konasana-Yoga-Pose-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Upavishta Konasana Yoga Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Upavishta Konasana Yoga Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bb1b26ea-6d1a-416e-ae3c-c8b3926c7860', 'Seated Front Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your front delts. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '3921201', '03921201-Dumbbell-Seated-Front-Raise_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Seated Front Raise. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Seated Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('bb259880-efab-4465-a054-3903a6fde3ad', 'Side Squat Jack', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Side Squat Jack builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '66771201', '66771201-Side-Squat-Jack-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. Ideal for quads strength and endurance.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Side Squat Jack', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bb2839cc-5e9c-4eeb-a2f2-b5a6d8217f6a', 'Jogging Jab', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. Your shoulders, core work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '104491201', '104491201-Jogging-Jab-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Jogging Jab. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'running', 'Jogging Jab', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bb3f3526-cb5e-4944-ad97-21a98c49088d', 'Side Lunge (Stick)', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this lunging exercise for quad development. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '92801201', '92801201-Stick-Side-Lunge-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Step to the side, bending that knee while keeping the other leg straight. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. Great for building strength in your quads.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Stick Side Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bb444021-3a6d-440c-b059-8582cf769936', 'Medicine Ball Sit Up Against Wall (Medicine Ball)', 'Core', 'Medicine Ball, Wall', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Lower Chest"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '6251201', '06251201-Medicine-Ball-Sit-up-(wall)_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.532804+00', '1. Hold a medicine ball at the appropriate position for Medicine Ball Sit Up. 2. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Medicine Ball Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bb4d825f-ed6b-4c07-bd23-2a73d9cb6f82', 'Decline Chest Fly (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Decline Bench', '{"Chest","Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Decline Fly is a flying exercise that targets your chest muscles. The front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '69941201', '69941201-Dumbbell-Decline-Fly-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Decline Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Fly', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Decline Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('bb59dcfd-77cd-4800-bc1c-a058d729dedd', 'Pec Deck Fly (Machine)', 'Chest', 'Fly Machine', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This flying exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '10301201', '10301201-Lever-Pec-Deck-Fly_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.87243+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Pec Deck Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Lever Pec Deck Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('bb5ecdaf-69fc-4742-9998-beda6b42f2ba', 'Belt Romanian Deadlift (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Lever Machine', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this hip hinge movement focusing on your hamstrings/glutes. The glutes, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '94941201', '94941201-Lever-Belt-Romanian-Deadlift_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.689343+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Belt Romanian Deadlift. 2. Push your hips back, lowering the weight along your legs with a flat back. 3. Lower until you feel a stretch in your hamstrings. 4. Drive hips forward to stand, squeezing glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Lever Belt Romanian Deadlift', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('bb6087e6-bb39-45a7-a081-074c892aded3', 'Side Plank Raise And Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Side Plank Raise And Crunch is a core raising exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '72561201', '72561201-Side-Plank-Raise-and-Crunch-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'side_plank', 'Side Plank Raise And Crunch', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bb705356-9330-4988-bd4c-50ea05b7bb70', 'Decline Crossing Sit Up (Decline Bench)', 'Core', 'Decline Bench', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Your shoulders, core work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The decline position targets the lower portion of the muscles more intensely. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '98221201', '98221201-Decline-Cross-Sit-up-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Decline Cross Sit Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Sit Up', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Decline Cross Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bb75e058-86d4-4edc-91e5-c41d6a55d1c6', 'Assisted Lying 90 Degrees Bent Knee Hip Adduction (Stability Ball)', 'Legs', 'Stability Ball', '{"Inner Thighs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your adductors. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. The stability ball adds an instability challenge that activates more stabilizer muscles. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '100131201', '100131201-Ball-Assisted-Lying-90-degrees-Bent-Knee-Hip-Addu.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Assisted Lying 90 Degrees Bent Knee Hip Adduction. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Assisted Lying 90 Degrees Bent Knee Hip Adduction. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 24, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_adduction', 'Assisted Lying 90 Degrees Bent Knee Hip Adduction', 'hip_abduction, squat, lunge', FALSE, 'stability_ball', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bb765eb1-de3b-45f1-9dc1-1863b1eeb009', 'Hyperextension On Bench (Hyperextension Bench)', 'Back', 'Hyperextension Bench', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This extension exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. Secondary activation of your hamstrings, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '4881201', '04881201-Hyperextension-(on-bench)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Raise your torso by extending at the lower back/hips. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Hyperextension', 'good_morning, bird_dog, superman', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bb794046-6f8e-4313-a0db-362bdb1931b5', 'Kneeling High Low Anti Rotation Chop (Cable)', 'Core', 'Cables', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Cable Kneeling High Low Anti Rotation Chop is a core rotation exercise that primarily targets your core. The obliques assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '75841201', '75841201-Cable-Kneeling-High-Low-Anti-Rotation-Chop-(male)_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.847006+00', '1. Set the cable pulley to the highest position and attach your preferred handle. 2. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Cable Kneeling High Low Anti Rotation Chop. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Kneeling High Low Anti Rotation Chop', 'woodchop, plank, dead_bug', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('bb972545-136e-4a25-ba12-756c4d4f9f6d', 'Seated Jump Rope Knee Tuck (Jump Rope)', 'Core', 'Jump Rope, Chair', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this jumping exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Your quads, calves work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '72641201', '72641201-Sitting-Jump-Rope-Knee-Tuck-on-Chair-(male)_Plyome.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'jump_rope', 'Seated Jump Rope Knee Tuck On Chair', 'running, jumping_jack, high_knees', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('bba3b2b1-21bf-443c-95ec-8de43d1a6476', 'Bicep Curl Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Full Body', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads","Glutes","Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this curling movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '106481201', '106481201-Dumbbell-Biceps-Curl-Squat-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Biceps Curl Squat. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 100, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bicep_curl', 'Biceps Curl Squat', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('bbb0823c-c81d-414d-8483-45ef9c400b27', 'Twist Chest Out', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This dynamic twisting movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements. A staple exercise that belongs in most training programs.', '60891201', '60891201-Twist-Chest-Out-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Twist Chest Out. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Twist Chest Out', 'bench_press, chest_fly, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bbb7e937-658a-46d5-bd52-394a426d2b7e', 'Seated Side Neck Stretch', 'Neck', 'Bodyweight', '{"Neck"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your neck with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. The upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '85611201', '85611201-Sitting-Side-Neck-Stretch-(VERSION-2)-(female)_Str.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Side Neck Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Switch sides and repeat for equal time. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'neck_stretch', 'Seated Side Neck Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bbc7ca4a-0f67-4de1-8147-6c69c97760c7', 'Lying Prone W', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this movement movement targeting your core. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function. This is a great exercise for all fitness levels with proper scaling.', '80951201', '80951201-Lying-Prone-W-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie face down with your body in a straight line. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Prone W. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Prone W', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bbe2f46f-0487-43b7-8fd1-8676eebb8be2', 'Kneeling Leg Half Circle', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Kneeling Leg Half Circle is a lower body movement exercise that targets your delts. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '48141201', '48141201-Kneeling-Leg-Half-Circle-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Get into a half-kneeling position (one knee down, opposite foot forward). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Leg Half Circle. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Kneeling Leg Half Circle', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bbe62be0-2b29-46ce-bf2b-d421990d53b7', 'Single Arm Swing (Kettlebell)', 'Full Body', 'Kettlebell', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Core"}'::text[], 'This full-body swinging exercise challenges multiple muscle groups simultaneously. Secondary activation of your glutes, core provides additional muscle engagement. The kettlebell''s offset center of mass increases the stability challenge. Compound movements like this develop coordination, power, and overall fitness.', '45271201', '45271201-Kettlebell-Single-Arm-Swing-(female)_Weightlifts_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Single Arm Swing. 2. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 3. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 4. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 53, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Single Arm Swing', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('bbea5e63-c93d-4a30-a971-76d02e817b5f', 'T Spine Opener', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The T Spine Opener is a flexibility exercise that targets your spine, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Your lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '78861201', '78861201-T-spine-opener-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for T Spine Opener. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cycling', 'T Spine Opener', 'running, elliptical, rowing_cardio', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bbf50caf-73dd-4586-90d1-c284187f2275', 'Side To Side (garland Pose) Frog Squat Into Forwar', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '84121201', '84121201-Side-to-Side-(Garland-Pose)-Frog-Squat-into-Forwar.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout. Ideal for quads strength and endurance.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Side To Side  Frog Squat Into Forwar', 'Side To Side Frog Squat Into Forwar', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bc14bb3f-f627-46db-ab9f-f565a4a5e66e', 'Lying Pelvic Tilt', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Lying Pelvic Tilt provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '72941201', '72941201-Lying-Pelvic-Tilt-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Pelvic Tilt. 2. Move into the stretch position for Lying Pelvic Tilt. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Pelvic Tilt', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bc2015f9-dbcc-41c9-ba26-48c6884353c6', 'Hammer Grip Incline Bench Two Arm Row (Kettlebell)', 'Back', 'Kettlebell, Incline Bench', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. You''ll also feel your biceps, rear delts working to support the movement. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '68381201', '68381201-Kettlebell-Hammer-Grip-Incline-Bench-Two-Arm-Row_B.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.504261+00', '1. Position two kettlebells for Kettlebell Hammer Grip Incline Bench Two Arm Row. 2. Set the bench to an incline angle (30-45 degrees). 3. Use a hammer/neutral grip with palms facing each other throughout. 4. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 5. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 6. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 81, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'incline_press', 'Hammer Grip Incline Bench Two Arm Row', 'bench_press, shoulder_press, chest_fly', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('bc298c0c-90d9-485f-8f05-2c5f21680ed5', 'Seated Stacked Arm Lift (Chair)', 'Chest', 'Chair', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this movement movement that develops pressing power. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '91081201', '91081201-Sitting-Stacked-Arm-Lift-on-a-Chair-(female)_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Seated Stacked Arm Lift On A Chair', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bc2b08b3-80f8-450c-b0b7-80a6b91554fd', 'Chest Press (TRX)', 'Chest', 'TRX', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '10731201', '10731201-Suspender-Chest-Press-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.340041+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Chest Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Suspender Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('bc2c7d9b-9476-4dc2-b67c-70906a97ac41', 'Front Elbow Plank', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'This stabilization exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your shoulders, lower back working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '90061201', '90061201-Front-Elbow-Plank-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your core engaged for stability. This exercise is excellent for abs development. Variation: Front Elbow Plank.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Front Elbow Plank', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bc3364ff-9cbe-4f26-ad53-31f440545948', 'Pike (TRX)', 'Core', 'TRX', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Suspender Pike is a lower body movement exercise that targets your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Works well as both a primary exercise or accessory movement.', '10851201', '10851201-Suspender-Pike-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Pike. 2. Set up in the starting position for Suspender Pike. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 40, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Suspender Pike', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('bc5376e2-f460-4699-9430-2fe559ab8cd3', 'Lying Triceps Extension Skull Crusher (Kettlebell)', 'Arms', 'Kettlebell', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this extension exercise for bigger arms. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. The kettlebell''s offset center of mass increases the stability challenge. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '58611201', '58611201-Kettlebell-Lying-Triceps-Extension-Skull-Crusher_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.689343+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Lying Triceps Extension Skull Crusher. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Kettlebell Lying Triceps Extension Skull Crusher. 3. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 4. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Lying Triceps Extension Skull Crusher', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('bc5af8f4-aebc-4ae0-9b07-9d45fb057350', 'Reverse Wrist Curl (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Cable Reverse Wrist Curl strengthens your forearms and grip through a curling motion. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '2101201', '02101201-Cable-Reverse-Wrist-Curl_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.667107+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Reverse Wrist Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'wrist_curl', 'Reverse Wrist Curl', 'hammer_curl, wrist_curl, bicep_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('bc84c175-19a8-475e-91ca-d7e52b6e9d8d', 'Curl - Close Grip (EZ Bar)', 'Arms', 'EZ Bar', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '4461201', '04461201-EZ-Barbell-Close-grip-Curl_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.123147+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for EZ Barbell Close Grip Curl. 2. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'EZ Curl - Close Grip', 'EZ Curl - Close Grip', FALSE, 'ez_bar', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('bcae3598-e591-466c-bee5-ba9044bbfbc1', 'Single Leg Standing Shoulder Press (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. The triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '85271201', '85271201-Dumbbell-Single-Leg-Standing-Shoulder-Press-(male).mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 89, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Single Leg Standing Shoulder Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('bcbaacae-d791-4d2b-be45-753e9732ffff', 'Muscle Up', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Muscle Up is a movement exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. Secondary activation of your chest, triceps provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '6311201', '06311201-Muscle-Up_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Muscle Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your lats. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 5, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Muscle Up', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bcc11e45-b004-4219-916b-ce3a0b365ca9', 'Double Snatch (Kettlebell)', 'Shoulders', 'Kettlebell', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Your quads, shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '5291201', '05291201-Kettlebell-Double-Snatch_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.483269+00', '1. Position two kettlebells for Kettlebell Double Snatch. 2. Explosively pull the weight from the floor/hang position. 3. As it rises, pull yourself under and catch it overhead with locked arms. 4. Stand to complete the lift. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'snatch', 'Double Snatch', 'power_snatch, clean, overhead_press', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('bcc6b0f2-7dc1-4cc7-9561-9fa7ffbc6893', 'Seated Ankle Circle (anti Clockwise)', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Seated Ankle Circle (anti Clockwise) provides a deep stretch for your delts, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '83781201', '83781201-Seated-Ankle-Circle-(Anti-Clockwise)-(female)_Stre.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Ankle Circle. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Ankle Circle', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bcc7cae2-8f45-4afd-b901-cda179a925e6', 'Standing Single Side Leg Raise (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Standing Single Side Leg Raise Chair Supported is a lower body raising exercise that targets your hip abductors. You''ll also feel your glutes working to support the movement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '86421201', '86421201-Standing-Single-Side-Leg-Raise-Chair-Supported-(fe.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 4. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Standing Single Side Leg Raise Chair Supported', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bcdb8e94-3ec2-4c3a-ad3a-ef29dae36c03', 'Under Knee Clap - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Alternating Under Knee Clap, focusing on your abs. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '104471201', '104471201-Alternating-Under-Knee-Clap-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.36063+00', '1. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 2. Set up in the starting position for Alternating Under Knee Clap. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Under Knee Clap - Alternating', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bce0d649-730c-4d63-b1e2-17b2075c340a', 'Bottoms Up', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '1381201', '01381201-Bottoms-Up-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.991486+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Bottoms Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bottoms_up', 'Bottoms Up', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bcf33cb6-0390-46ad-a4aa-abcb046cdca9', 'Russian Twist With Hands On Chest', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Russian Twist With Hands On Chest targets your obliques through a twisting motion, building rotational core strength. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '46461201', '46461201-Russian-Twist-with-Hands-on-Chest-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Russian Twist With Hands On Chest. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Russian Twist With Hands On Chest', 'crunch, plank, leg_raise, wood_chop', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bcfa5030-995e-45b8-be20-b9b5418dc5b9', 'Standing Tibialis Anterior Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This stretching movement focuses on your gastrocnemius and soleus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '67731201', '67731201-Standing-Tibialis-Anterior-Stretch-(female)_Calves.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Tibialis Anterior Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your calves. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Standing Tibialis Anterior Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bcfd6776-da02-450a-af9d-597ce5becf63', 'Opposite Arm And Leg Raise (Against Wall)', 'Core', 'Wall', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this raising movement focusing on your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '72161201', '72161201-Opposite-Arm-and-Leg-Raise-against-Wall-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.71819+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Opposite Arm And Leg Raise Against Wall', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bd11f79b-1a79-49ec-8c88-69765b1549b3', 'Standing Twisting Side Leg Kick Tap', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Standing Twisting Side Leg Kick Tap is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic twisting movements. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '103071201', '103071201-Standing-Twisting-Side-Leg-Kick-Tap-(female)_Plyo.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Twisting Side Leg Kick Tap. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 44, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Standing Twisting Side Leg Kick Tap', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bd1d604a-153c-4cc2-9aa6-17fe4f4bfe70', 'Seated Side Bend Stretch (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Seated Side Bend Stretch On A Chair provides a deep stretch for your obliques, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '104711201', '104711201-Seated-Side-Bend-Stretch-on-a-Chair-(male)_Stretc.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Side Bend Stretch On A Chair. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 6. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 27, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Seated Side Bend Stretch On A Chair', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bd4837b9-1983-4f4a-8fe5-0621a2e3566b', 'Standing Bent Arm Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Standing Bent Arm Lateral Raise is a raising exercise that targets your lateral delts for shoulder development. The standing position engages your core for stability. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '23161201', '23161201-Dumbbell-Standing-Bent-Arm-Lateral-raise-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Bent Arm Lateral Raise. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 94, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Standing Bent Arm Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('bd561125-f99e-4e57-bd99-e4a8f38a4d22', 'Walking On Spot', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Walking On Spot (front Pov) builds reactive power and improves conditioning. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '81741201', '81741201-Walking-On-Spot-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Walking On Spot. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Walking On Spot', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bd5780ee-38da-4960-b8a9-500113d78284', 'Side Lying T Thigh Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this raising movement focusing on your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '58351201', '58351201-Side-Lying-T-Thigh-Raise-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Side Lying T Thigh Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bd5a1893-2868-4c52-8811-e8da8f023a28', 'Rear Delt Raise (Barbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Barbell', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your rear delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Your upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '26371201', '26371201-Barbell-Rear-Delt-Raise-(female)_shoulder.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Rear Delt Raise. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides and back, focusing on rear delts. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Shoulder Horizontal Abduction', 'Pull', 'Isolation', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated)', 'Wide', 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Rear Delt Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, face_pull, bent_over_row', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('bd665eeb-2ed1-4d8c-89cc-e6ba837bd9ed', 'Rotate Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Rotate Push Up is a core pushing exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '6821201', '06821201-Rotate-Push-up-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain a neutral spine throughout. An effective movement for your core routine.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Rotate Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bd718c59-ae6e-4b90-8d86-d53a97569b74', 'Step On Spot', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Step On Spot is a cardiovascular exercise that improves endurance and heart health. You''ll also feel your quads working to support the movement. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight.', '57481201', '57481201-Step-on-Spot-(female)_Cardio_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Step On Spot. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Step On Spot', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bd757cff-dd04-4da2-97a9-00e9a726455c', 'Ring Straddle L Sit (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Core', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Ring Straddle L Sit is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '75131201', '75131201-Ring-Straddle-L-Sit-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.937212+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Ring Straddle L Sit. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 38, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'groin_stretch', 'Ring Straddle L Sit', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('bd7ff892-5c12-40c4-ab0e-43cb2b442165', 'Kneeling Elbow Supported Downward Dog', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your full body, the Kneeling Elbow Supported Downward Dog helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. The hamstrings, calves, shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '95521201', '95521201-Kneeling-Elbow-Supported-Downward-Dog-(female)_Str.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Move into the stretch position for Kneeling Elbow Supported Downward Dog. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Kneeling Elbow Supported Downward Dog', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bd873923-7d47-4d4e-a9be-ffd0dfc43270', 'Kneeling Preacher Curl (Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band, Preacher Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '70411201', '70411201-Band-Kneeling-Preacher-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Kneeling Preacher Curl. 2. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'preacher_curl', 'Kneeling Preacher Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('bd8a1710-d678-497b-bf41-5c739964b14a', 'Bent Over Twisting Row (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Bent Over Twisting Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Bending over allows gravity to provide resistance in a different plane. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '94071201', '94071201-Dumbbell-Bent-over-Twisting-Row-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Bent Over Twisting Row. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 74, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Bent Over Twisting Row', 'lat_pulldown, pull_up, bicep_curl, face_pull, seated_row', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('bd8f00fc-b061-47ab-b205-1a0aa1741fa5', 'Explosive Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pushing movement that develops pressing power. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '54601201', '54601201-Explosive-Push-Up_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Perform the concentric (lifting) phase explosively with maximum effort. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Explosive Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bda251b7-8725-40b2-bcd3-d6efa5234ce5', 'Bicep Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '24831201', '24831201-Dumbbell-Biceps-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Biceps Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('bda51a5b-131b-4bb6-aa4f-a96e6f2c0dbd', 'Spine Stretch Forward_pilates', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Spine Stretch Forward_pilates is a flexibility exercise that targets your spine, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Secondary activation of your lower back provides additional muscle engagement. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '28731201', '28731201-Spine-Stretch-Forward_Pilates_Pilates.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.153182+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Spine Stretch Forward_pilates. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Spine Stretch Forward_pilates', 'running, elliptical, rowing_cardio', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bda6e4d7-6664-4923-b5b6-775d9fdc5619', 'Lying Knee Extension (Pilates Machine)', 'Legs', 'Pilates Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your quads, the Pilates Machine Lying Knee Extension helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '106551201', '106551201-Pilates-Machine-Lying-Knee-Extension-(female)_Str.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Pilates Machine Lying Knee Extension. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Pilates Machine Lying Knee Extension. 3. Extend through the target joint(s) for Pilates Machine Lying Knee Extension.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_extension', 'Pilates Lying Knee Extension', 'Pilates Lying Knee Extension', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('bdac0098-0716-4ce3-85f8-ec7bd36b092b', '4 Corners Side Step', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This full-body stepping exercise challenges multiple muscle groups simultaneously. You''ll also feel your quads working to support the movement. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '58071201', '58071201-4-Coners-Side-Step-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for 4 Corners Side Step. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', '4 Corners Side Step', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bdb3ba0a-a6dd-42c0-bcbb-b1cb406841d2', 'Side Bend (Kettlebell)', 'Core', 'Kettlebell', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Side Bend is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '73591201', '73591201-Kettlebell-Side-Bend_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Side Bend. 2. Set up in the starting position for Kettlebell Side Bend. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Side Bend', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('bdb6b9a8-2a94-4abe-9574-6398f2c74268', 'Seated Arm Circle - Underhand (Chair)', 'Shoulders', 'Chair', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Seated Underhand Arm Circle On A Chair, an effective shoulder movement exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '86551201', '86551201-Seated-Underhand-Arm-Circle-on-a-Chair-(male)_Shou.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.123147+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Use an underhand (supinated) grip with palms facing up/toward you. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Seated Underhand Arm Circle On A Chair', 'Seated Arm Circle On A Chair - Underhand', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bdc0cf36-fa7a-4ea6-97c3-a8af3613fde3', 'Stepjack Inner Biceps Curl', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This dynamic curling movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '56291201', '56291201-Stepjack-Inner-Biceps-Curl-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 80, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Stepjack Inner Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bdca6c8d-e9f2-4c0a-9eb4-9c008202a2c1', 'Arm Crossover Curtsy', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Arm Crossover Curtsy is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. Secondary activation of your front delts provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '66421201', '66421201-Arm-Crossover-Curtsy-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Arm Crossover Curtsy. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Arm Crossover Curtsy', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bdd4c2f7-7086-4d24-ab9f-eab9a74770d6', 'Side Lying Cycle Oblique Tuck', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Side Lying Cycle Oblique Tuck, focusing on your abs. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '85141201', '85141201-Side-Lying-Cycle-Oblique-Tuck-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Lying Cycle Oblique Tuck. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'core_exercise', 'Side Lying Cycle Oblique Tuck', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bddb86e1-692c-4c32-9911-a748eadb4674', 'Hands Behind Head Side Leg Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your glutes working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '93481201', '93481201-Hands-Behind-Head-Side-Leg-Raise-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 2. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Hands Behind Head Side Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bdded97c-3b3a-4056-ab68-d90da75d5ec1', 'Shoulder Internal Rotation At 90 Abductio (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Shoulder Internal Rotation At 90 Abductio is a rotation exercise that targets your rotator cuff for shoulder development. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '97331201', '97331201-Dumbbell-Shoulder-Internal-Rotation-at-90-Abductio.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Shoulder Internal Rotation At 90 Abductio. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Dumbbell Shoulder Internal Rotation At 90 Abductio. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Shoulder Internal Rotation At 90 Abductio', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('bde296f3-e963-4077-b0cd-b32419f25bf7', 'Standing Single Arm Chest Press (Cable)', 'Chest', 'Cables', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Cable Standing Single Arm Chest Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '98161201', '98161201-Cable-Standing-Single-Arm-Chest-Press_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Single Arm Chest Press. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Standing Single Arm Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('bde57958-cda4-4b14-82a3-14b453a225b7', 'Step Up Opposite Elbow To Knee Twist (Step Platform)', 'Legs', 'Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build your aerobic capacity with this steady-state cardio movement. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight.', '8001201', '08001201-Step-Up-Opposite-Elbow-To-Knee-Twist-(female)_Card.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Step Up Opposite Elbow To Knee Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'step_up', 'Step Up Opposite Elbow To Knee Twist', 'lunge, split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bde799ea-9bb2-49a2-a405-4086b3eadd92', 'Otis Up', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities. A staple exercise that belongs in most training programs.', '6411201', '06411201-Otis-Up_waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Otis Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Otis Up', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bde7f6a8-2329-45cc-86a9-9bd4a0b5ffe6', 'Hip Internal Rotation Test', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your hips, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '67881201', '67881201-Hip-Internal-Rotation-Test-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Hip Internal Rotation Test. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Move into the stretch position for Hip Internal Rotation Test. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Hip Internal Rotation Test', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bde9c3e1-3428-4f20-9f85-df60e0dd8870', 'Side Lying Raise On Floor (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '91901201', '91901201-Dumbbell-Side-Lying-Raises-on-Floor-(female)_Shoul.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Side Lying Raises On Floor. 2. Position yourself on the floor for Dumbbell Side Lying Raises On Floor. 3. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 4. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 5. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Side Lying Raise On Floor', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('be012610-2df8-4925-bcdf-800b21039df9', 'Romanian Deadlift (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Cable Romanian Deadlift is a lower body hip hinge exercise that targets your hamstrings/glutes. You''ll also feel your glutes, lower back working to support the movement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '65521201', '65521201-Cable-Romanian-Deadlift-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Romanian Deadlift. 2. Push your hips back, lowering the weight along your legs with a flat back. 3. Lower until you feel a stretch in your hamstrings. 4. Drive hips forward to stand, squeezing glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Romanian Deadlift', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('be09de5f-c94c-4a31-916f-ef4504fbdd07', 'High Knee Skips', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Calves"}'::text[], 'Enhance your stamina and burn calories with this effective cardio movement. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness.', '30911201', '30911201-High-Knee-Skips-(male)_Cardio-FIX2_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for High Knee Skips. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'high_knees', 'High Knee Skips', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('be1eb79b-6465-48bc-bd8c-70f286c8f7a3', 'Decline Triceps Extension (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Decline Bench', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this extension exercise for bigger arms. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '3061201', '03061201-Dumbbell-Decline-Triceps-Extension_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Decline Triceps Extension. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', 'Extension', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Decline Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('be23d383-d475-46a0-b219-1812a417845a', 'Standing Elbows Tucked Open And Close', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this movement movement targeting your full body. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '72241201', '72241201-Standing-Elbows-Tucked-Open-and-Close-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.570929+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Elbows Tucked Open And Close. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Elbows Tucked Open And Close', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('be2a565e-d6ec-4cd1-8fba-b63c33d56169', 'Front Raise (Kettlebell)', 'Shoulders', 'Kettlebell', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'Target your front delts with the Kettlebell Front Raise, an effective shoulder raising exercise. The kettlebell''s offset center of mass increases the stability challenge. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '69321201', '69321201-Kettlebell-Front-Raise-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Front Raise. 2. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('be320c4a-09ef-4f8d-bcbb-c6960dc36e75', 'Half Frog Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Target your full body with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness. Progress gradually by increasing resistance over time.', '96841201', '96841201-Half-Frog-Stretch-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Half Frog Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Half Frog Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('be393a11-b577-4249-b055-5beda03ae088', 'Double Lean Back Quadriceps Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Double Lean Back Quadriceps Stretch provides a deep stretch for your quads, ideal for recovery and mobility work. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '84391201', '84391201-Double-Lean-Back-Quadriceps-Stretch-(female)_Stret.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Double Lean Back Quadriceps Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Double Lean Back Quadriceps Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('be4535ae-df5e-4b04-bde4-7fe070a8bb01', 'Walking Front Kick Reach Up', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity kicking exercise that challenges your entire body. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. A staple exercise that belongs in most training programs.', '93691201', '93691201-Walking-Front-Kick-Reach-Up-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Walking Front Kick Reach Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Walking Front Kick Reach Up', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('be4c2b58-0051-4d21-8787-621bc3b79c55', 'Seated Side Step Row (Chair)', 'Back', 'Chair', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This dynamic rowing movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Secondary activation of your quads provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '91221201', '91221201-Sitting-Side-Step-Row-on-Chair-(female)_Plyometric.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 3. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 4. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 5. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 6. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 7. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Side Step Row On Chair', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('be59838d-079c-4958-96ff-1d313fe4b14d', 'Glute Bridge Chest Press', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pressing movement that develops pressing power. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '80561201', '80561201-Bodyweight-Glute-Bridge-Chest-Press-(female)_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 2. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Glute Bridge Chest Press', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('be66cd59-3ad2-46f8-a521-f8da49a88a1c', 'Pendulum Leg Plus', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. Focus on controlled form throughout each repetition.', '86371201', '86371201-Pendulum-Leg-Plus-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Pendulum Leg Plus. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Pendulum Leg Plus', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('be727bf8-e379-434a-b69b-7abb54b75cc1', 'Toe Squat Yoga Pose', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target your quads with this squatting stretch that helps restore range of motion. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '78351201', '78351201-Toe-Squat-Yoga-Pose-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Toe Squat Yoga Pose', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('be81e2db-6919-41c0-bdca-60d9d8a798cd', 'High Lunge To Warrior I Pose', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target your quads with this lunging stretch that helps restore range of motion. Your hips, shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '79701201', '79701201-High-Lunge-to-Warrior-I-Pose-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Move into the stretch position for High Lunge To Warrior I Pose. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 70, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'High Lunge To Warrior I Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('be8d4c93-6c0f-4b73-b832-f067608b38c3', 'Seated Chest Fly (Machine)', 'Chest', 'Fly Machine', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This flying exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. The front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '22551201', '22551201-Lever-Seated-Fly-(female)_Chest-FIX2_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.724336+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Fly. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 4. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 5. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form. Great for building strength in your chest.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Lever Seated Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('be921be4-37cf-4723-a9ec-5d2025c83ff2', 'Prone Incline Twist Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '87951201', '87951201-Dumbbell-Prone-Incline-Twist-Curl_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.083517+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Prone Incline Twist Curl. 2. Lie face down (prone position) for Dumbbell Prone Incline Twist Curl. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Prone Incline Twist Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('be9b3b90-a459-45ff-8c1b-558c23fe1d96', 'Incline Push Up - Reverse Grip', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pushing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '4941201', '04941201-Incline-Reverse-Grip-Push-Up_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Use a reverse grip (opposite of the standard grip for this exercise). 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Incline Push Up - Reverse Grip', 'Incline Push Up - Reverse Grip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('beaaea8c-f364-4c88-a755-052740583241', 'Pull Through (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this pulling movement that emphasizes the glutes. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '12061201', '12061201-Cable-pull-through_hips.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Pull Through. 2. Set up in the starting position for Cable Pull Through. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_through', 'Pull Through', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('beb3be8e-9f0e-4a11-89e0-9acb7bbe74d9', 'Seated Back Twist', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Seated Back Twist targets your obliques through a twisting motion, building rotational core strength. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '51301201', '51301201-Seated-Back-Twist-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Seated Back Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Seated Back Twist', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('beb70b54-c77c-4d86-88e0-e9fa7ad089bc', 'Lying Chest Press (Plate Loaded)', 'Chest', 'Chest Press Machine', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Lever Lying Chest Press (plate Loaded), an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '10411201', '10411201-Lever-Lying-Chest-Press-(plate-loaded)_Chest-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Lying Chest Press. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lever Lying Chest Press. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Lever Lying Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('beba5222-ed28-48a1-a782-fe54beb09c40', 'Rolling Back', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Target your back with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. Your shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '28591201', '28591201-Rolling-Back-(female)_Pilates_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Rolling Back. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Rolling Back', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bec4cf94-88ea-4f0a-a222-dd6fb9042f7f', 'Downward Facing Dog Adho Mukha Svanasana', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Downward Facing Dog Adho Mukha Svanasana is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '9491201', '09491201-Downward-Facing-Dog-Adho-Mukha-Svanasana-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Downward Facing Dog Adho Mukha Svanasana. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Downward Facing Dog Adho Mukha Svanasana', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bec7b418-29f0-4818-ac05-ea9ded726764', 'Single Arm Lateral Raise (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your lateral delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '89011201', '89011201-Cable-Single-Arm-Lateral-Raise-(VERSION-2)-(male)_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Single Arm Lateral Raise. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Single Arm Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('beca7c01-1aad-4a7b-9b4d-a828002d7c1d', 'Side Lying Lateral Costal Breathing', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '99781201', '99781201-Side-Lying-Lateral-Costal-Breathing-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Lying Lateral Costal Breathing. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'breathing', 'Side Lying Lateral Costal Breathing', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bed3e394-a1e8-495a-aed4-df474db9fef7', 'Standing Bicep Curl (Plate)', 'Arms', 'Weight Plate', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '66981201', '66981201-Weighted-Plate-Standing-Biceps-Curl-(male)_Forearm.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Weighted Plate Standing Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'plate', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bed46a89-531f-4bba-89db-00a5faa78635', 'Push Up Mountain Climber', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This dynamic pushing movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your hip flexors, shoulders working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '90301201', '90301201-Push-up-Mountain-Climber-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'mountain_climber', 'Push Up Mountain Climber', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip, tricep_pushdown', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bef1f3cd-621b-42cc-9bd1-94018f8a7744', 'Side Bend Stretch (Stick)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Stick Side Bend Stretch is a core stretching exercise that primarily targets your abs. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '54051201', '54051201-Stick-Side-Bend-Stretch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Stick Side Bend Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Stick Side Bend Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bf0fa88b-b57d-457e-8e40-f4b720fa32cd', 'Side Lying Legs Lift', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your hip abductors. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '93341201', '93341201-Side-Lying-Legs-Lift-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Lying Legs Lift. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your hip abductors. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Side Lying Legs Lift', 'crunch, plank, russian_twist, hanging_knee_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bf1fd19b-3cfc-439b-898f-8d6e0b00ea44', 'Seated Floor Toe Touch - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Seated Floor Alternating Toe Touch is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '93421201', '93421201-Sitting-Floor-Alternating-Toe-Touch_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.123147+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Seated Floor Alternating Toe Touch. 2. Sit on the floor with your legs positioned as required. 3. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'toe_touch', 'Seated Floor Toe Touch - Alternating', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bf530fd6-7c08-4920-90db-6a223b56e0ff', 'Seated Bicep Curl (Chair)', 'Arms', 'Chair', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '104811201', '104811201-Seated-Biceps-Curl-on-Chair-(male)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 67, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Seated Biceps Curl On Chair', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bf65ff98-7a03-413e-a322-82b60cdbb4b6', 'Seated Calf Press (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Calf Raise Machine', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Lever Seated Calf Press isolates your calf muscles through a pressing motion. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '23351201', '23351201-Lever-Seated-Calf-Press_Calves.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Calf Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Execute the pressing motion for Lever Seated Calf Press, extending through the target muscles. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your core engaged for stability. This variation specifically emphasizes the calves.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Lever Seated Calf Press', 'standing_calf_raise, seated_calf_raise, tibialis_raise', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('bf6ac4d5-b088-4925-9a7c-8dd74b0db063', 'Side Walk Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Side Walk Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '67431201', '67431201-Side-Walk-Squat-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Side Walk Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bf7577e0-41db-4327-bfab-6e8a202bf776', 'Arm Tuck Side Bend', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this movement movement targeting your obliques. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '63791201', '63791201-Arm-Tuck-Side-Bend-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Arm Tuck Side Bend. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your obliques. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Arm Tuck Side Bend', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bf75b422-a1da-4f48-b4df-2d3c305e0789', 'Chair Squat Calf Rock (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Chair Squat Calf Rock isolates your calf muscles through a squatting motion. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '87571201', '87571201-Chair-Squat-Calf-Rock-(female)_Calves_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Chair Squat Calf Rock', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bfa8f24c-3f7b-4212-907e-263097ffd754', 'Seated Bicep Curl (Dumbbell) - Alternating', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '11961201', '11961201-Dumbbell-Alternate-Biceps-Curl_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Alternate Biceps Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Biceps Curl - Alternating', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('bfaf7602-23d7-4619-9936-d9d800af71fc', 'Stepback With Coner Touch (Cones)', 'Legs', 'Cones', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic stepping movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Your quads work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '55911201', '55911201-Stepback-with-Coner-Touch-(Male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Stepback With Coner Touch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Stepback With Coner Touch', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bfb6dcd3-aa2d-4a69-829a-d0876af3b540', 'Seated Upper Body Rotation', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This rotation movement focuses on your obliques for a complete core workout. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '51291201', '51291201-Seated-Upper-Body-Rotation-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Seated Upper Body Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Upper Body Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bfc528d8-6561-4b7d-927d-49175f041c75', 'Reverse Crunch Leg Drop', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '82321201', '82321201-Reverse-Crunch-Leg-Drop-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Lift your hips off the floor by contracting your lower abs. 2. Bring your knees toward your chest, then lower with control. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Reverse Crunch Leg Drop', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bfc8eb40-823d-40a3-ac85-2b6cd63e46bb', 'Russian Twist With Legs Supported (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Russian Twist With Legs Supported targets your obliques through a twisting motion, building rotational core strength. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '103931201', '103931201-Dumbbell-Russian-Twist-with-Legs-Supported_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Russian Twist With Legs Supported. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Dumbbell Russian Twist With Legs Supported. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Russian Twist With Legs Supported', 'crunch, plank, leg_raise, wood_chop', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('bfc9393e-708b-41e3-989e-2b7dbf94f4ac', 'Warrior I To Warrior II Pose', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Core"}'::text[], 'Target your full body with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. The hips, shoulders, quads assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '79711201', '79711201-Warrior-I-to-Warrior-II-Pose-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Warrior I To Warrior II Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 50, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Warrior I To Warrior II Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bfcdf43d-ea8e-4f04-85ac-3fc5b3a6e4cc', 'KAS Glute Bridge (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this bridging movement focused on hip extension. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '55541201', '55541201-Dumbbell-KAS-Glute-Bridge-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell KAS Glute Bridge. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'KAS Glute Bridge', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('bfcfc365-d729-4d2b-b2f5-d6c32f743078', 'Single Arm Upright Row (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell One Arm Upright Row is a rowing exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. You''ll also feel your traps working to support the movement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '3631201', '03631201-Dumbbell-One-Arm-Upright-Row_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Pull the weight straight up along your body, leading with your elbows. 3. Raise until elbows reach shoulder height, then lower with control. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'upright_row', 'Single Arm Upright Row', 'bent_over_row, lat_pulldown, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('bfdb3e58-e3db-4be9-89e6-fd14ee624b92', 'Single Arm Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pushing movement that develops pressing power. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '7251201', '07251201-Single-Arm-Push-up_Chest-FIX2_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Single Arm Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('bffd6f97-7ad4-4d38-9099-ccea1d756e28', 'Standing Side Glute Raise (Against Wall)', 'Core', 'Wall', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Standing Side Glute Raise Against Wall is a lower body raising exercise that targets your core. The standing position engages your core for stability. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '86571201', '86571201-Standing-Side-Glute-Raise-against-Wall-(female)_Hi.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.870314+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 64, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Standing Side Glute Raise Against Wall', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c00a98ab-333c-4354-8a70-b61e4d8243a8', 'Inchworm Front Arm Tap', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '87781201', '87781201-Inchworm-Front-Arm-Tap-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Inchworm Front Arm Tap. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'inchworm', 'Inchworm Front Arm Tap', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('c012cfe8-096a-4b8a-9ebb-50209b1d0fcd', 'Standing Wood Chopper (Resistance Band)', 'Core', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Work your side abdominals with this movement exercise that strengthens your obliques. Secondary activation of your shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '80451201', '80451201-Resistance-Band-Standing-Wood-Chopper-(female)_Wai.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Standing Wood Chopper. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 57, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'woodchop', 'Standing Wood Chopper', 'russian_twist, pallof_press, cable_crunch', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('c02376a2-d844-49b3-986f-d646d0bba04c', 'Standing Quadriceps Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your quads, the Standing Quadriceps Stretch helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '10591201', '10591201-Standing-Quadriceps-Stretch_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.737494+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Move into the stretch position for Standing Quadriceps Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Standing Quadriceps Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c02d545c-df2f-4e65-80d3-fc6110d66c4f', 'High Plank Shoulder Tap', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this stabilization movement that works your abs. You''ll also feel your shoulders, lower back working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '80181201', '80181201-High-Plank-Shoulder-Tap-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your core engaged for stability. Ideal for abs strength and endurance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'High Plank Shoulder Tap', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c02d788b-6c16-46c6-861a-bba0299fb505', 'Curl (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Cable Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '8681201', '08681201-Cable-Curl-(male)_Upper-Arms-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('c02ebd6b-0ffc-459d-a907-246bf3b2f01a', 'Single Arm Crossover (Cable)', 'Full Body', 'Cables', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Core"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. Your shoulders, core work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '69491201', '69491201-Cable-Single-Arm-Crossover-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Single Arm Crossover. 2. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Single Arm Crossover', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('c0356977-ddd6-43cb-b334-519c393cf05a', 'Preacher Swing Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Preacher Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '86131201', '86131201-Dumbbell-Preacher-Swing-Curl-(male)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Preacher Swing Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Preacher Swing Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c03f764c-781c-4910-87b3-ddbfd964b713', 'Lying Crunch (Straight Legs)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '60041201', '60041201-Lying-Crunch-(straight-legs)-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Crunch. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Lying Crunch', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c04497c6-0791-4179-9e35-a3ee234d7fcf', 'Standing Balance Hip Abduction', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your glute med/abductors. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '57441201', '57441201-Standing-Balance-Hip-Abduction-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.425788+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Balance Hip Abduction. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glute med/abductors. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Standing Balance Hip Abduction', 'hip_adduction, glute_bridge, clamshell', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c05c3019-8d29-447a-825f-d4a3c4fa9a1f', 'Lying (side) Quadriceps Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your quads, the Lying (side) Quadriceps Stretch helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '6131201', '06131201-Lying-(side)-Quadriceps-Stretch_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.847006+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Move into the stretch position for LyingQuadriceps Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Lying  Quadriceps Stretch', 'Lying Quadriceps Stretch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c06018f4-8341-47e9-99f1-a0fb92ed8373', 'Ring Maltese Cross (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Full Body', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Core"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Ring Maltese Cross builds reactive power and improves conditioning. You''ll also feel your shoulders, core working to support the movement. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '76161201', '76161201-Ring-Maltese-Cross-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Ring Maltese Cross. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 5, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Ring Maltese Cross', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('c0726929-91a0-44a1-8807-24977bbe3079', 'Side Bridge With Bent Leg', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this bridging movement focused on hip extension. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '106851201', '106851201-Side-Bridge-with-Bent-Leg-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Side Bridge With Bent Leg', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c07ec4aa-bc49-49af-9d8c-decbd277d715', 'Lunge (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this lunging exercise for quad development. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '22181201', '22181201-Dumbbell-Lunge-(female)_Thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lunge. 2. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c0a2afaa-686d-4fb5-99d4-c2185e2db721', 'Standing Arms Circling - Alternating', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Standing Alternate Arms Circling, an effective shoulder movement exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '32591201', '32591201-Standing-Alternate-Arms-Circling-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Standing Arms Circling - Alternating', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c0ae157c-fc55-4358-ab52-c42e44d82790', 'Seated Side To Side Neck Bend (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Target your core with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '105571201', '105571201-Seated-Side-to-Side-Neck-Bend-on-Chair-(male)_Str.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Side To Side Neck Bend On Chair. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 6. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'neck_exercise', 'Seated Side To Side Neck Bend On Chair', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c0b5b4c5-f7bb-4596-8f2f-e6add572a86d', 'Standing Wood Chopper (Cable)', 'Core', 'Cables', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement movement focuses on your obliques for a complete core workout. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '80471201', '80471201-Cable-Standing-Wood-Chopper-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Wood Chopper. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'woodchop', 'Standing Wood Chopper', 'russian_twist, pallof_press, cable_crunch', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('c0b9a0bb-7fd3-4772-a788-905c40103b21', 'Straight Back Stiff Leg Deadlift (Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this hip hinge movement focusing on your hamstrings/glutes. The glutes, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '57501201', '57501201-Band-Straight-Back-Stiff-Leg-Deadlift-(female)_Hip.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.887491+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Straight Back Stiff Leg Deadlift. 2. Push your hips back, lowering the weight along your legs with a flat back. 3. Lower until you feel a stretch in your hamstrings. 4. Drive hips forward to stand, squeezing glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Straight Back Stiff Leg Deadlift', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('c0c15239-b92e-4622-b1e4-12d1ce51dd13', 'Double Push Press (Kettlebell)', 'Shoulders', 'Kettlebell', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The kettlebell''s offset center of mass increases the stability challenge. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements. A staple exercise that belongs in most training programs.', '5281201', '05281201-Kettlebell-Double-Push-Press_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Position two kettlebells for Kettlebell Double Push Press. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Double Push Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('c0c66699-b544-4d2d-b7dd-a3a87abd6cbc', '3 Point Standing Hops', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'The 3 Point Standing Hops is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. The standing position engages your core for stability. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '76801201', '76801201-3-Point-Standing-Hops-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.847006+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for 3 Point Standing Hops. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 52, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hop', '3 Point Standing Hops', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c0cb883a-10a6-44aa-9419-d6ca0b2dd3b2', 'Prone Incline Curl (Barbell)', 'Arms', 'Barbell, Incline Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '721201', '00721201-Barbell-Prone-Incline-Curl_Upper-Arms-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Prone Incline Curl. 2. Lie face down (prone position) for Barbell Prone Incline Curl. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', 'Isolation', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, 'Underhand (Supinated)', 'Standard', 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'incline_curl', 'Prone Incline Curl', 'bicep_curl, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('c0cc5897-6ce6-408f-8657-b3ea376de252', 'Ring Reverse Ab Rollout (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Core', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Ring Reverse Ab Rollout, focusing on your abs. The lats, shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '48201201', '48201201-Ring-Reverse-Ab-Rollout_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Ring Reverse Ab Rollout. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 38, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'ab_rollout', 'Ring Reverse Ab Rollout', 'plank, crunch, dead_bug', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('c0efe0c9-0516-465f-8458-0f9c33189460', 'Back Extension With Hands Behind Head (Stability Ball)', 'Back', 'Stability Ball', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Back Extension With Hands Behind Head (stability Ball) strengthens your lower back muscles through a controlled extension motion. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. The stability ball adds an instability challenge that activates more stabilizer muscles. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '28211201', '28211201-Exercise-Ball-Back-Extension-With-Hands-Behind-Hea.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.505723+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Back Extension With Hands Behind Head. 2. Raise your torso by extending at the lower back/hips. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Back Extension With Hands Behind Head', 'good_morning, bird_dog, superman', FALSE, 'stability_ball', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c0f6ecd5-0094-4aa0-963d-dc4cfbee6bf1', 'Two Arm Clean (Kettlebell)', 'Shoulders', 'Kettlebell', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Two Arm Clean is a movement exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. Your quads, glutes, traps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '5521201', '05521201-Kettlebell-Two-Arm-Clean_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Position two kettlebells for Kettlebell Two Arm Clean. 2. Explosively pull the weight upward from the starting position. 3. Pull yourself under the weight and catch it at shoulder level. 4. Stand to complete the lift, then lower with control. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'clean', 'Two Arm Clean', 'power_clean, deadlift, front_squat', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('c0fcfa23-6d38-40aa-bbf2-c9d26b558ebf', 'Ring Incline Plank (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Core', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this stabilization movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your shoulders, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '78781201', '78781201-Ring-Incline-Plank-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.123147+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 61, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Ring Incline Plank', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'gymnastic_rings', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('c10f5506-1cd0-4586-a9c2-20d353a3076d', 'Single Arm Overhead Triceps Extension (Resistance Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Single Arm Overhead Triceps Extension targets your triceps through a extension motion. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '91321201', '91321201-Resistance-Band-Single-Arm-Overhead-Triceps-Extens.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Single Arm Overhead Triceps Extension. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Single Arm Overhead Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('c111b801-010e-4ddb-bf18-04ee1100d5a7', 'Seated Dynamic Chest Stretch (Chair) - Alternating', 'Chest', 'Chair', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your chest, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Secondary activation of your shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '86151201', '86151201-Seated-Alternate-Dynamic-Chest-Stretch-on-a-Chair-.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.483269+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Alternate Dynamic Chest Stretch On A Chair. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 6. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 27, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_stretch', 'Seated Dynamic Chest Stretch On A Chair - Alternating', 'stretch_shoulder, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c11c884b-8aed-413f-a60b-720c368628a3', 'Vertical Leg Raise On Parallel Bars (Dip Bars)', 'Core', 'Dip Bars', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this raising movement focusing on your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '8261201', '08261201-Vertical-Leg-Raise-(on-parallel-bars)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 2. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Vertical Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, russian_twist, hanging_knee_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c121b573-ab7a-49be-9704-41b92d01bc71', 'Single Leg Slam (Medicine Ball)', 'Legs', 'Medicine Ball', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Medicine Ball Single Leg Slam builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '76121201', '76121201-Medicine-Ball-Single-Leg-Slam-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Hold a medicine ball at the appropriate position for Medicine Ball Single Leg Slam. 2. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Medicine Ball Single Leg Slam', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'medicine_ball', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c12aac04-fa5a-4d78-b89a-53655efb9219', 'Lying Lat Row', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Lying Lat Row is a rowing exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. Secondary activation of your biceps, rear delts provides additional muscle engagement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '90381201', '90381201-Lying-Lat-Row-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Lat Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Lying Lat Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c12eff0a-365d-45dc-a2f4-9241272c0135', 'Twist And Turn Punch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Twist And Turn Punch is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic twisting movements. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '54951201', '54951201-Twist-and-Turn-Punch-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Twist And Turn Punch. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Twist And Turn Punch', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c12f164e-72e2-4535-8e5a-30cf3b002b02', 'Diagonal Stepback And Reach', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic stepping movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Your quads work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '80391201', '80391201-Diagonal-Stepback-and-Reach-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Diagonal Stepback And Reach. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Diagonal Stepback And Reach', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c13af847-1f93-455a-948c-6e68d71b0f0d', 'Seated Bicep Curl (Dumbbell) - Alternating', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '37611201', '37611201-Dumbbell-Seated-Alternate-Biceps-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Seated Alternate Biceps Curl. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 94, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Seated Biceps Curl - Alternating', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c13d2d48-411e-42f1-8d23-4431a9c58d21', 'Bicep Curl - Single Arm (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '97321201', '97321201-Cable-One-Arm-Inner-Biceps-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arm.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable One Arm Inner Biceps Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Single Arm Inner Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('c168b837-02f7-4c47-b2e2-b8cc70885e57', 'Swing Clean Grip Front Squat Overhead Press (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Quads","Glutes","Core"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Develop functional strength with the Kettlebell Swing Clean Grip Front Squat Overhead P, a comprehensive squatting exercise. The glutes, core assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '53351201', '53351201-Kettlebell-Swing-Clean-grip-Front-Squat-Overhead-P.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Swing Clean Grip Front Squat Overhead P. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 83, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Swing Clean Grip Front Squat Overhead Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('c169b74c-6efa-4cd6-b62d-ccbad67c1b9f', 'Wrist Reverse Curl (Barbell)', 'Arms', 'Barbell', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{"Biceps"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Wrist Reverse Curl strengthens your forearms and grip through a curling motion. You''ll also feel your biceps working to support the movement. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '791201', '00791201-Barbell-Wrist-Reverse-Curl-(VERSION-2)_Forearms-FI.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Wrist Reverse Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Wrist Reverse Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('c172f869-0a96-4518-ba74-49fed83b7530', 'Assisted Underhand Chin Up - Close Grip (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. The biceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '25431201', '25431201-Assisted-Close-grip-Underhand-Chin-up-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 2. Pull yourself up, focusing on bicep and lat engagement. 3. Raise until chin is over the bar, lower with full control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Assisted Underhand Chin Up - Close Grip', 'Assisted Underhand Chin Up - Close Grip', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c17652a8-4ad6-4ca3-8e16-c152feb2d613', 'High Row (Machine)', 'Back', 'Row Machine', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Lever High Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Secondary activation of your biceps, rear delts provides additional muscle engagement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '106381201', '106381201-Lever-High-Row-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.991486+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever High Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'cable_row', 'Lever High Row', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('c18ac128-1d10-46c8-b24a-0b08cd3d1dfa', 'Narrow Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads","Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Narrow Squat is a rowing exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '87201201', '87201201-Dumbbell-Narrow-Squat-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Narrow Squat. 2. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Narrow Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c190d05e-839a-445f-a022-4dae209f9207', 'Standing Stacked Arms Lift', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This movement exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts. This variation is excellent for building mind-muscle connection. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '85561201', '85561201-Standing-Stacked-Arms-Lift-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Stacked Arms Lift. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Standing Stacked Arms Lift', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c19bb05c-73aa-49f7-94e3-720447c745a8', 'Standing External Rotation (Resistance Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This rotation exercise works your rotator cuff for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The standing position engages your core for stability. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '64411201', '64411201-Resistance-Band-Standing-External-Rotation-(female.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Standing External Rotation. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Resistance Band Standing External Rotation. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Standing External Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('c19e45cf-cf36-480e-bdcb-b5f8653b03e8', 'Lying Arms Forward Circle', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Lying Arms Forward Circle, an effective shoulder movement exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '90011201', '90011201-Lying-Arms-Forward-Circle-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.010404+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Arms Forward Circle. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Arms Forward Circle. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Lying Arms Forward Circle', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c1a34532-ab04-4364-83aa-cd08c587605e', 'Bar Grip Sumo Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads","Glutes"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength. Excellent for pre-exhausting the target muscle before compound lifts.', '24301201', '24301201-Dumbbell-Bar-Grip-Sumo-Squat-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Bar Grip Sumo Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Bar Grip Sumo Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c1a9fb1c-0f06-408a-bbcf-92565ccdc659', 'Lying Hyperextension Abduction (Resistance Band)', 'Back', 'Resistance Band, Hyperextension Bench', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This extension exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. You''ll also feel your hamstrings, lower back working to support the movement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '72111201', '72111201-Resistance-Band-Lying-Hyperextension-Abduction-(fe.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.128549+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Lying Hyperextension Abduction. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Resistance Band Lying Hyperextension Abduction. 3. Raise your torso by extending at the lower back/hips. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Lying Hyperextension Abduction', 'good_morning, bird_dog, superman', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('c1b0bfba-f5dc-408f-afce-53758838b02f', 'Forearm Supination', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Forearm Supination strengthens your forearms and grip through a movement motion. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '106921201', '106921201-Forearm---Supination-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Forearm Supination. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your forearms. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Forearm Supination', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c1b86d8a-fdb0-4e47-a8ea-54b4335a004b', 'Seated Celebratory Speed Torso Twist (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Seated Celebratory Speed Torso Twist On Chair. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '104951201', '104951201-Seated-Celebratory-Speed-Torso-Twist-on-Chair-(ma.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Seated Celebratory Speed Torso Twist On Chair. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Seated Celebratory Speed Torso Twist On Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c1bb58b8-ae9c-4456-8669-b1c738303ca5', 'Single Leg Hamstring Bridge (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Single Leg Hamstring Bridge targets your hamstrings through a controlled bridging motion. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '93591201', '93591201-Single-Leg-Hamstring-Bridge-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 33, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Single Leg Hamstring Bridge', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('c1c56d66-562e-4f26-bc47-3706c18e600b', 'Lying Single Arm Pronated Triceps Extension (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this extension exercise for bigger arms. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '3441201', '03441201-Dumbbell-Lying-One-Arm-Pronated-Triceps-Extension_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Lying One Arm Pronated Triceps Extension. 3. Use an overhand (pronated) grip with palms facing down/away. 4. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 5. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Lying Single Arm Pronated Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c1de28f1-31e5-476a-b64d-2d5a72cf9b77', 'Seated Ankle Dorsi Flexion', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Ankles"}'::text[], '{"Calves"}'::text[], 'Target your ankles with this flexion stretch that helps restore range of motion. You''ll also feel your calves working to support the movement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '100021201', '100021201-Sitting-Ankle-Dorsi-Flexion-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.628647+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Ankle Dorsi Flexion. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Ankle Dorsi Flexion', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c207f91c-ee24-47f6-9abc-7aa0cce8847f', 'Cross Body Twisting Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This crunching movement focuses on your obliques for a complete core workout. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '2631201', '02631201-Cross-Body-Twisting-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shoulder_stretch', 'Cross Body Twisting Crunch', 'plank, leg_raise, russian_twist, sit_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c20c77c7-6600-461d-923c-58fe2c26af6d', 'Sit Up', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Sit Up, focusing on your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '7361201', '07361201-Sit-Up_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.628647+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Sit Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c211104e-c87a-4c70-a9b1-0f4990146559', 'Roll Front Shoulder And Chest Lying On Floor', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Roll Front Shoulder And Chest Lying On Floor is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '54171201', '54171201-Roll-Front-Shoulder-and-Chest-Lying-on-Floor-(fema.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Roll Front Shoulder And Chest Lying On Floor. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Roll Front Shoulder And Chest Lying On Floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_exercise', 'Roll Front Shoulder And Chest Lying On Floor', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c230ba3f-f43d-4a89-9fe2-58b5ea86fdfa', 'Wrist Ulnar Deviation With Elbow Suppor', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Wrist Ulnar Deviation With Elbow Suppor strengthens your forearms and grip through a movement motion. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '84681201', '84681201-Bodyweight-Wrist-Ulnar-Deviation-with-Elbow-Suppor.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.60311+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Bodyweight Wrist Ulnar Deviation With Elbow Suppor. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your forearms. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 40, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Wrist Ulnar Deviation With Elbow Suppor', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c23d8ff7-f401-4220-abc6-4ca79e9cfb49', 'Seated Shoulders Circle - Alternating', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Seated Alternate Shoulders Circle, an effective shoulder movement exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '89431201', '89431201-Seated-Alternate-Shoulders-Circle-(male)_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Seated Shoulders Circle - Alternating', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c24d6249-f8e5-49e6-b0a0-7ed012a931ba', 'Switching Downward Punch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Switching Downward Punch is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. Your shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '57101201', '57101201-Switching-Downward-Punch-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Switching Downward Punch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Switching Downward Punch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c25269a7-dbb6-42fa-9785-49ccd1f12127', 'Renegade Row (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. Your biceps, rear delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '29811201', '29811201-Dumbbell-Renegade-Row-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Renegade Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'dumbbell_row', 'Renegade Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c2555680-b966-4e20-b8b1-55b42ff1313a', 'Basic To Cross Donkey Kick', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this kicking movement that emphasizes the glutes. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '63161201', '63161201-Basic-to-Cross-Donkey-Kick-(female)_Hips-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Basic To Cross Donkey Kick. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glutes. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Basic To Cross Donkey Kick', 'hip_thrust, glute_bridge, leg_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c2609e2c-415e-4b2f-9dd5-1945a4e13f43', 'Fish Pose Matsyasana', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Fish Pose Matsyasana is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '9501201', '09501201-Fish-Pose-Matsyasana-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.505723+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Fish Pose Matsyasana. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Fish Pose Matsyasana', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c27b117b-3df8-4cb3-911c-5b32cb366ee5', 'Pullback Side Leg Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This dynamic pulling movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '97881201', '97881201-Pullback-Side-Leg-Raise-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 2. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum. Perfect for targeting your abs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Pullback Side Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c28435ed-38e7-4578-8292-55f693f051ff', 'Military Press Russian Twist With Legs Floor Off (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Military Press Russian Twist With Legs Floor Off targets your obliques through a pressing motion, building rotational core strength. The triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '68061201', '68061201-Dumbbell-Military-Press-Russian-Twist-with-Legs-Floor-Off-(VERSION-2)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.71819+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Military Press Russian Twist With Legs Floor Off. 2. Position yourself on the floor for Dumbbell Military Press Russian Twist With Legs Floor Off. 3. Execute the pressing motion for Dumbbell Military Press Russian Twist With Legs Floor Off, extending through the target muscles. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 87, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Military Press Russian Twist With Legs Floor Off', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c2918dc8-a5d2-478c-993d-1108ce500c9d', 'Side Bridge (Bent Knee)', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This bridging exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '7011201', '07011201-Side-Bridge-(bent-knee)-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Side Bridge', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c291a18e-a418-4237-b7a8-b4746f1b56f9', 'Ring Handstand (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Shoulders', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Ring Handstand is a movement exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '75191201', '75191201-Ring-Handstand-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Ring Handstand. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 5, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Ring Handstand', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('c292996a-8705-4a67-ae7c-da947945b26c', 'Plank Walk Up', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'This stabilization exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Your shoulders, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '27931201', '27931201-Plank-Walk-Up-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction. Ideal for abs strength and endurance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Plank Walk Up', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
