('c296f574-d71b-4917-8de5-4655a8f7b36b', 'Standing Behind Back Shoulders Press (Dumbbell)', 'Full Body', 'Dumbbells', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your full body. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '55211201', '55211201-Dumbbell-Standing-Behind-Back-Shoulders-Press_Shou.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Behind Back Shoulders Press. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Standing Behind Back Shoulders Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c29989eb-b2e1-47de-9c02-34bf9e383dc7', 'Russian Twist (Medicine Ball)', 'Core', 'Medicine Ball', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Russian Twist (with Medicine Ball). Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '12471201', '12471201-Russian-Twist-(with-medicine-ball)_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Hold a medicine ball at the appropriate position for Russian Twist. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Russian Twist. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Russian Twist', 'crunch, plank, leg_raise, wood_chop', FALSE, 'medicine_ball', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c2a1f718-1f99-44a7-bfeb-76700efa118f', 'Seated Single Straight Leg Raise A Chair (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '91261201', '91261201-Sitting-Single-Straight-Leg-Raise-a-Chair-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 4. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Seated Single Straight Leg Raise A Chair', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c2ab3714-ee89-4d3b-9b5f-f53e1a6168c7', 'Overhead Clap', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Overhead Clap, an effective shoulder movement exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '46651201', '46651201-Overhead-Clap-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Overhead Clap. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Overhead Clap', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c2acf24e-1f1c-4c43-add3-a4594a51b845', 'Side Step Arms Rainbow', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Side Step Arms Rainbow is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic stepping movements. Your quads work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '81691201', '81691201-Side-Step-Arms-Rainbow-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Step Arms Rainbow. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Side Step Arms Rainbow', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c2c72427-50f6-493b-b7ac-d4917fb8a3c7', 'Standing Chest Fly (Cable) - Alternating', 'Chest', 'Cables', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this flying movement that develops pressing power. You''ll also feel your front delts working to support the movement. The standing position engages your core for stability. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '79871201', '79871201-Cable-Standing-Alternate-Chest-Fly_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Alternate Chest Fly. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 4. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 5. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 6. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 7. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Standing Chest Fly - Alternating', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('c2c87f90-b3a8-4f09-acde-4f3e4d98440b', 'Leg Front Kick', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this kicking movement that works your abs. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '50821201', '50821201-Leg-Front-Kick-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Leg Front Kick. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Leg Front Kick', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c2dcca30-5ef1-4cfc-86c6-a9b29dd60183', 'Power Pull (TRX)', 'Back', 'TRX', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats"}'::text[], 'The Suspender Power Pull is a pulling exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. The lats assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '10861201', '10861201-Suspender-Power-Pull-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Power Pull. 2. Perform the concentric (lifting) phase explosively with maximum effort. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 40, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Suspender Power Pull', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('c2e15f10-5f82-4623-acc1-162a2c589ad3', 'Angled Press (Kettlebell)', 'Shoulders', 'Kettlebell', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. The triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '70991201', '70991201-Kettlebell-Angled-Press-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Angled Press. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Angled Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('c2e341f9-b16a-4215-a8b4-cdd308a1a8df', 'Ring Single Leg Curl (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings, Towel', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This curling movement works your hamstrings for balanced leg development. Your calves work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '78731201', '78731201-Ring-Single-Leg-Curl-with-towel_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 2. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 3. Extend legs back out with control. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control. A solid choice for legs day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 63, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Ring Single Leg Curl With Towel', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('c2fe9212-c7ab-4ee7-b008-8ecc0eacfa8b', 'Rear Lateral Raise Support Head (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Rear Lateral Raise (support Head) is a raising exercise that targets your lateral delts for shoulder development. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '3791201', '03791201-Dumbbell-Rear-Lateral-Raise-(support-head)_Shoulde.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Rear Lateral Raise. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Rear Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c304bc32-0ca0-4377-b678-3ebc0ba621ce', 'Twisting Knee Up', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Twisting Knee Up is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic twisting movements. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '55321201', '55321201-Twisting-Knee-Up-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Twisting Knee Up. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Twisting Knee Up', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c305727d-a109-4a13-9401-3b94684829b6', 'Table Top Bridge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this bridging movement that emphasizes the glutes. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '71721201', '71721201-Table-Top-Bridge-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. This exercise is excellent for glutes development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Table Top Bridge', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c30ec98e-cbd9-4af4-af9b-65c225be05c7', 'Assisted Triceps Dip Kneeling (Dip Bars)', 'Arms', 'Dip Bars', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Assisted Triceps Dip (kneeling) targets your triceps through a dipping motion. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '191201', '00191201-Assisted-Triceps-Dip-(kneeling)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 3. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Assisted Triceps Dip', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c315b78b-aeb7-4fe3-bd9e-0c787a265024', 'Seated Single Calf Press (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Calf Raise Machine', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Lever Seated Single Calf Press isolates your calf muscles through a pressing motion. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '71771201', '71771201-Lever-Seated-Single-Calf-Press-(female)_Calves_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.855778+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Single Calf Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Execute the pressing motion for Lever Seated Single Calf Press, extending through the target muscles. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Lever Seated Single Calf Press', 'standing_calf_raise, seated_calf_raise, tibialis_raise', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('c31653a1-71b8-4d7d-9440-3210d6e3c1c5', 'Arms Overhead Full Sit Up', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Arms Overhead Full Sit Up is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '32041201', '32041201-Arms-Overhead-Full-Sit-up-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Arms Overhead Full Sit Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'neck_stretch', 'Arms Overhead Full Sit Up', 'crunch, leg_raise, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c3184bc6-ca9b-494d-9ec1-77eb412255df', 'Prone Cobra Palms Under Thighs', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Prone Cobra Palms Under Thighs is a lower body movement exercise that targets your lower back. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '32061201', '32061201-Prone-Cobra-Palms-Under-Thighs-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Lie face down (prone position) for Prone Cobra Palms Under Thighs. 2. Set up in the starting position for Prone Cobra Palms Under Thighs. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your lower back. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 50, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Prone Cobra Palms Under Thighs', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c31f883e-a3f0-479c-8029-ece39356ca16', 'Half Kneeling Side Lunge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs"}'::text[], 'Target your quads with this lunging stretch that helps restore range of motion. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '89871201', '89871201-Half-Kneeling-Side-Lunge-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Get into a half-kneeling position (one knee down, opposite foot forward). 2. Step to the side, bending that knee while keeping the other leg straight. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Half Kneeling Side Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c321d0e5-8cd5-4206-a898-8d35d7676cd4', 'Standing Butt Kick', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Calves"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity kicking exercise that challenges your entire body. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '57971201', '57971201-Standing-Butt-Kick-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.425788+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Butt Kick. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Standing Butt Kick', 'high_knees, jumping_jack, running', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c3293856-be71-4fcf-b242-2a1fa979cd57', 'Seated Good Morning (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Seated Good Morning targets your hamstrings through a controlled movement motion. You''ll also feel your glutes, lower back working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '95151201', '95151201-Dumbbell-Sitting-Good-Morning-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.483269+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Seated Good Morning. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Seated Good Morning', 'romanian_deadlift, back_extension, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c32cdad0-12df-42ec-a808-cd1d1f56d35e', 'Seated Heel Slide (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Seated Heel Slide On A Chair isolates your calf muscles through a movement motion. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '84271201', '84271201-Seated-Heel-Slide-on-a-Chair-(male)_Calves_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.249384+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Heel Slide On A Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c33d073b-6e39-4b71-aac4-9b1d42dde0e8', 'Seated Chest Press (Cable)', 'Chest', 'Cables', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Cable Seated Chest Press, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '79261201', '79261201-Cable-Seated-Chest-Press-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Seated Chest Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Seated Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('c343dd51-4232-4757-8bd1-138a6da08ad6', 'Bent Over Single Arm Kickback - Neutral Grip (Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this kicking movement that emphasizes the glutes. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The bent over position requires core engagement to maintain a neutral spine. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '104061201', '104061201-Band-Bent-over-One-Arm-Neutral-grip-Kickback-(mal.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Bent Over One Arm Neutral Grip Kickback. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Use a neutral grip with palms facing each other. 4. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 5. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Bent Over Single Arm Kickback - Neutral Grip', 'Bent Over One Arm Kickback - Neutral Grip', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('c346c2f1-0653-4bc6-ad08-3b5468df4487', 'Bent Leg Side Kick Kneeling (Resistance Band)', 'Core', 'Resistance Band', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Resistance Band Bent Leg Side Kick (kneeling), focusing on your core. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '103941201', '103941201-Resistance-Band-Bent-Leg-Side-Kick-(kneeling)-(ma.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.991486+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Bent Leg Side Kick. 2. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 47, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Bent Leg Side Kick', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('c36b0641-5d3b-4af4-9b3d-d3411dd8a02f', 'Weighted Lying Flat Hip Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Weighted Dumbbell Lying Flat Hip Raise, focusing on your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '73791201', '73791201-Weighted-Dumbbell-Lying-Flat-Hip-Raise-(male)_Wais.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Weighted Dumbbell Lying Flat Hip Raise. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Weighted Dumbbell Lying Flat Hip Raise. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Weighted Dumbbell Lying Flat Hip Raise. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Weighted Lying Flat Hip Raise', 'Weighted Lying Flat Hip Raise', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c37184e4-a480-4501-bd33-42c9a97c49e2', 'Kater Hop (Medicine Ball)', 'Legs', 'Medicine Ball', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '107581201', '107581201-Medicine-Ball-Skater-Hop-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Hold a medicine ball at the appropriate position for Medicine Ball Skater Hop. 2. Set up in the starting position for Medicine Ball Skater Hop. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'skater', 'Medicine Ball Skater Hop', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'medicine_ball', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c3730900-c56d-407c-9178-6e891321bf49', 'Seated Lower Back Stretch - Twisting', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your lower back, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. You''ll also feel your glutes working to support the movement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '104541201', '104541201-Sitting-Lower-Back-Stretch-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Lower Back Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Seated Lower Back Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c3736a4a-026a-4213-981c-84b8453207b2', 'Front Raise Rope (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'The Cable Front Raise (rope Attachment) is a raising exercise that targets your front delts for shoulder development. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '73711201', '73711201-Cable-Front-Raise-(rope-attachment)-(male)_Shoulde.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.608253+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Front Raise. 2. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('c37f32d1-f3a2-439a-b250-554821cb512e', 'Walking On Spot Sky Reach', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Walking On Spot Sky Reach builds reactive power and improves conditioning. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '98391201', '98391201-Walking-on-Spot-Sky-Reach-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Walking On Spot Sky Reach. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'shoulder_stretch', 'Walking On Spot Sky Reach', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c3879c33-1944-45f4-ab89-de77be52c626', 'Somersault Stand Up', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Somersault Stand Up, focusing on your abs. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '74611201', '74611201-Somersault-Stand-up-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Somersault Stand Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Somersault Stand Up', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c38ccfcc-aae1-4d46-a836-e23ad267c9ef', 'Side Lying Quadriceps Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target your quads with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '84381201', '84381201-Side-Lying-Quadriceps-Stretch-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Move into the stretch position for Side Lying Quadriceps Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Side Lying Quadriceps Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c390041a-695a-4871-8311-7a54d96bd8a8', 'Standing Cat Cow Stretch', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your spine, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Your core work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '90631201', '90631201-Standing-Cat-Cow-Stretch-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.570929+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Move into the stretch position for Standing Cat Cow Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Standing Cat Cow Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c3963ca2-d589-4c63-bd7b-7cf7e253bb16', 'Stepback Arms Back Raise', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this raising exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. You''ll also feel your quads working to support the movement. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '97861201', '97861201-Stepback-Arms-Back-Raise-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Stepback Arms Back Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Stepback Arms Back Raise', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c3963e7c-e583-4fb1-839b-8600e3b1ec45', 'Double Diagonal Reach', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements. Maintain proper breathing - exhale during the effort phase.', '57651201', '57651201-Double-Diagonal-Reach-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Double Diagonal Reach. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Double Diagonal Reach', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c3a4608b-51a3-4ad0-8776-edf9760d737d', 'Triceps Extension - Forward Push (Machine)', 'Arms', 'Tricep Extension Machine', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This extension movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '6071201', '06071201-Lever-Triceps-Extension_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Triceps Extension. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Lever Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('c3a8aeae-4111-4998-b3bb-dd56c22fa337', 'Circles Knee Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger calves with this targeted stretching exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '2571201', '02571201-Circles-Knee-Stretch_Calves.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Circles Knee Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your calves. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'knee_stretch', 'Circles Knee Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c3af8cb4-4b3a-4e5f-a1e8-d14de0d9179e', 'Standing Bicep Curl - Rope (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. The standing position engages your core for stability. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '106451201', '106451201-Cable-Standing-Biceps-Curl-(rope-attachment)_Uppe.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Biceps Curl. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Standing Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('c3b0f903-0def-4b4e-884c-03271b60f5b2', 'Ring Archer Pull Up (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Back', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Ring Archer Pull Up is a pulling exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. Your biceps, upper back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '75121201', '75121201-Ring-Archer-Pull-up-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Pull yourself up by driving your elbows down and back. 2. Continue until your chin clears the bar, then lower with control to a full hang. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Ring Archer Pull Up', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('c3b7e7cd-ca63-48a3-8e23-18063876899d', 'Twisting Woodchopper', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This dynamic twisting movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '75751201', '75751201-Twisting-Woodchopper-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Twisting Woodchopper. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 42, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'woodchop', 'Twisting Woodchopper', 'russian_twist, pallof_press, cable_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c3c8ef1b-ecf6-454b-8a91-1c7649c7a1e2', 'Concentration Extension On Knee (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Cable Concentration Extension (on Knee) targets your triceps through a extension motion. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '1521201', '01521201-Cable-Concentration-Extension-(on-knee)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Concentration Extension. 2. Extend through the target joint(s) for Cable Concentration Extension. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Concentration Extension', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('c3d28c8f-422d-42f3-b37d-a9d061d3716c', 'Criss Cross Upper Chest Raise', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity raising exercise that challenges your entire body. Secondary activation of your shoulders, core provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '76361201', '76361201-Criss-Cross-Upper-Chest-Raise-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Criss Cross Upper Chest Raise. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Criss Cross Upper Chest Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c3da8c12-24d4-4944-ae2c-d1ab75f2fb67', 'Lying Abduction (Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your glute med/abductors. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '24211201', '24211201-Resistance-Band-Lying-Abduction-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.128549+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Lying Abduction. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Resistance Band Lying Abduction. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Lying Abduction', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('c3e971cd-049b-4351-8325-552a92e78e1b', 'Incline Twist Press (Kettlebell)', 'Chest', 'Kettlebell, Incline Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pressing movement that develops pressing power. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '68421201', '68421201-Kettlebell-Incline-Twist-Press_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Incline Twist Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 81, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Incline Twist Press', 'bench_press, chest_fly, shoulder_press, decline_bench_press', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('c3f48c3e-ce64-463d-b77e-2463e1128b92', 'Reverse Preacher Curl (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Cable Reverse Preacher Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '2091201', '02091201-Cable-Reverse-Preacher-Curl_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.079801+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Reverse Preacher Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'preacher_curl', 'Reverse Preacher Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('c3f5c561-a798-4e82-b233-6fd68da7ddfe', 'Step Squat Jack', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Step Squat Jack builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '57071201', '57071201-Step-Squat-Jack-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Step Squat Jack', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c4051bcb-6f6c-4ae3-b097-df7db55e4d23', 'Adductors Stretch Transverse Plane', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Inner Thighs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Adductors Stretch Transverse Plane is a lower body stretching exercise that targets your adductors. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '76921201', '76921201-Adductors-Stretch-Transverse-Plane-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Adductors Stretch Transverse Plane. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your adductors. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_adduction', 'Adductors Stretch Transverse Plane', 'hip_abduction, squat, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c425e0b2-7d74-4357-82a1-ca25a64a66eb', 'Hanging Knee Raise (Pull-Up Bar) - Alternating', 'Core', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Hanging Alternating Knee Raise, focusing on your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. The hanging position challenges your grip while targeting the primary muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '107351201', '107351201-Hanging-Alternating-Knee-Raise-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Grip the bar and hang with arms fully extended, engaging your shoulders. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Hanging Alternating Knee Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Hanging Knee Raise - Alternating', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c42a3ea1-a7f4-49f8-aa38-cf9a569b705f', 'Standing Leg Slide Lunge (Towel)', 'Legs', 'Towel', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Standing Leg Slide Lunge With Towel is a lunging exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '43801201', '43801201-Standing-Leg-Slide-Lunge-with-Towel_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Standing Leg Slide Lunge With Towel', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c4340c67-187f-43f4-8cf0-7190c01679d4', 'Weighted Chains Bench Press (Barbell)', 'Chest', 'Barbell, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics. A staple exercise that belongs in most training programs.', '42011201', '42011201-Barbell-Weighted-Chains-Bench-Press-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.079801+00', '1. Load a barbell and set it on a bench rack at the appropriate height. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form. Include this in your chest training.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bench_press', 'Weighted Chains Bench Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('c444a00f-1b2c-4cda-920f-ec7926ccdc31', 'Single Leg Chair Squat (Smith Machine)', 'Legs', 'Smith Machine, Chair', '{Quadriceps}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '88041201', '88041201-Smith-Single-Leg-Chair-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.153182+00', '1. Set the Smith machine bar to the appropriate starting height for Smith Single Leg Chair Squat. 2. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 3. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 4. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 5. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Smith Single Leg Chair Squat', 'Single Leg Chair Squat', FALSE, 'smith_machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('c448eaba-e731-4e09-bfd5-ad587453a186', 'Doorway Chest Stretch (Door Frame)', 'Chest', 'Door Frame', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This stretching exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '75531201', '75531201-Doorway-Chest-Stretch-(male)_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Doorway Chest Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_stretch', 'Doorway Chest Stretch', 'stretch_shoulder, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c45a1087-1344-4113-a9ac-cfe18333c710', 'Curtsey Lunge (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this lunging exercise for quad development. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '81901201', '81901201-Barbell-Curtsey-Lunge-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Curtsey Lunge. 2. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Curtsey Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('c45be10e-d440-4afb-bd4c-8a3a96826d9d', 'Mountain Climber (Medicine Ball)', 'Core', 'Medicine Ball', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This climbing exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Your hip flexors, shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '75241201', '75241201-Medicine-Ball-Mountain-Climber-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.109351+00', '1. Hold a medicine ball at the appropriate position for Medicine Ball Mountain Climber. 2. From plank position, drive one knee toward your chest. 3. Quickly switch legs, bringing the other knee forward. 4. Continue alternating at a quick pace while maintaining plank form. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'mountain_climber', 'Medicine Ball Mountain Climber', 'burpee, plank, high_knees', TRUE, 'medicine_ball', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c45ed05b-fc6b-483a-8ec6-33a80425a0ae', 'Standing Wood Chopper (Resistance Band)', 'Core', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement movement focuses on your obliques for a complete core workout. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '80211201', '80211201-Resistance-Band-Standing-Wood-Chopper-(male)_Waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Standing Wood Chopper. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 57, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'woodchop', 'Standing Wood Chopper', 'russian_twist, pallof_press, cable_crunch', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('c4782210-1655-42ba-a890-e64acde403e9', 'Seated Back Stretch Both Hands To Feet', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Target your back with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. Your shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '82361201', '82361201-Seated-Back-Stretch-Both-Hands-To-Feet-(female)_St.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Back Stretch Both Hands To Feet. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Seated Back Stretch Both Hands To Feet', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c483079b-404f-4a32-9679-1d5072746c76', 'Hand Up Front Step', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity stepping exercise that challenges your entire body. Your quads work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '72731201', '72731201-Hand-up-Front-Step-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Hand Up Front Step. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Hand Up Front Step', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c491100e-ff1c-4add-ba6f-f7ce250787a9', 'Twist March', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this twisting exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '89051201', '89051201-Twist-March-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Twist March. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Twist March', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c498321b-bcce-4ee1-83cf-d6bb029784a6', 'Standing Y Raise (Resistance Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Secondary activation of your upper back provides additional muscle engagement. The standing position engages your core for stability. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '92861201', '92861201-Resistance-Band-Standing-Y-Raise-(female)_Shoulder.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Standing Y Raise. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Resistance Band Standing Y Raise. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Standing Y Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('c49e7b96-3eea-4e26-9b95-fbc29cc94fbf', 'Knee Tuck Row (TRX)', 'Back', 'TRX', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. Secondary activation of your biceps, rear delts provides additional muscle engagement. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '94991201', '94991201-Suspender-Knee-Tuck-Row-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Knee Tuck Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Suspender Knee Tuck Row', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('c49f0f88-b1ed-4e74-b5c4-0a30b7e1b96b', 'Seated Ankle Circle (clockwise)', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your ankles, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Secondary activation of your calves provides additional muscle engagement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '83771201', '83771201-Seated-Ankle-Circle-(Clockwise)-(female)_Stretchin.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Ankle Circle. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Seated Ankle Circle', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c4abf9ed-b5a8-4158-9381-606599ed11d5', 'Front Raise (Dumbbell) - Alternating', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your front delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '43411201', '43411201-Dumbbell-Alternate-Front-Raise-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Alternate Front Raise. 2. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Front Raise - Alternating', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c4b26929-c050-410c-862a-165227624218', 'Seated Pulse Row (Chair)', 'Back', 'Chair', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Seated Pulse Row On A Chair is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Your biceps, rear delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '91151201', '91151201-Sitting-Pulse-Row-on-a-Chair-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. At the bottom or top, pulse up and down in small movements before completing the rep. 7. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pulse', 'Seated Pulse Row On A Chair', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c4ba1745-7ecc-4b19-8edb-0cdeebb37e2c', 'Bear Walk', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Bear Walk, focusing on your abs. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '98321201', '98321201-Bear-Walk-(VERSION-2)-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Bear Walk. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Bear Walk', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c4c6ad5e-1be1-4b11-8e63-d6fb55488ac6', 'Curtsey Side Step', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Curtsey Side Step builds reactive power and improves conditioning. You''ll also feel your quads working to support the movement. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '80741201', '80741201-Curtsey-Side-Step-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.52454+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Curtsey Side Step. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Curtsey Side Step', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c4c7ee64-9640-4ca1-b55a-d775557034fd', 'High Knee Step Up (Step Platform)', 'Legs', 'Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this stepping exercise for quad development. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '4791201', '04791201-High-Knee-Step-up-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Step one foot onto the elevated surface. 3. Drive through that foot to lift your body up onto the platform. 4. Step back down with control and repeat. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'high_knees', 'High Knee Step Up', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c4c97d4f-7046-4070-8546-cdc4609b5954', 'Lying Vertical Scissors On Floor', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your core. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '64301201', '64301201-Lying-Vertical-Scissors-on-Floor-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Lying Vertical Scissors On Floor. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Vertical Scissors On Floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Vertical Scissors On Floor', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c4d7ca46-db27-44e6-8aa7-8552104a0a6c', 'Stepback Opposite Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Stepback Opposite Crunch builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '80271201', '80271201-Stepback-Opposite-Crunch-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Stepback Opposite Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c4e302ed-54f4-48f7-aef4-6d62e85acc5e', 'Double Woodchopper', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This movement movement focuses on your obliques for a complete core workout. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '91591201', '91591201-Double-Woodchopper-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Double Woodchopper. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your obliques. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'woodchop', 'Double Woodchopper', 'russian_twist, pallof_press, cable_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c4f00988-8f03-4af4-b6ff-9b57a036bd49', 'Frog Squat Into Forward Fold', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your adductors area and enhance overall flexibility. The hips assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '84131201', '84131201-Frog-Squat-into-Forward-Fold-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hamstring_stretch', 'Frog Squat Into Forward Fold', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c500f7a2-29cb-4767-a5cc-5bd366b7fd8b', 'Fast Sit Up Slow Down', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '81821201', '81821201-Fast-Sit-Up-Slow-Down-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Use a slow, controlled tempo throughout the entire range of motion. 2. Set up in the starting position for Fast Sit Up Slow Down. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Fast Sit Up Slow Down', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c5037102-9aa1-445d-9537-1b3dd5ca3844', 'Twisting Woodchopper', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This dynamic twisting movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '81841201', '81841201-Twisting-Woodchopper-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Twisting Woodchopper. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 42, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'woodchop', 'Twisting Woodchopper', 'russian_twist, pallof_press, cable_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c504dc01-4734-48fb-bd3b-2fd14ba7141a', 'Plank Hit The Ball - Alternating', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Plank Alternating Hit The Ball is a core stabilization exercise that primarily targets your abs. Your shoulders, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '105541201', '105541201-Plank-Alternating-Hit-the-Ball-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Plank Hit The Ball - Alternating', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c5085505-45ca-4804-8f09-3dbf97cb745b', 'Hanging Straight Leg Hip Raise (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Core', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Forearms"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Your hip flexors, grip work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Hanging adds a grip and core stability component to the exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '36041201', '36041201-Hanging-Straight-Leg-Hip-Raise-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Grip the bar and hang with arms fully extended, engaging your shoulders. 2. Set up in the starting position for Hanging Straight Leg Hip Raise. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Hanging Straight Leg Hip Raise', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c5098814-b7bc-49c4-b9df-aca0a5e9af57', 'Standing Side And Front Leg Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this raising movement focusing on your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '55061201', '55061201-Standing-Side-and-Front-Leg-Raise_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Standing Side And Front Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c51328c4-5867-4ea7-8442-7ba72349d3fc', 'Standing Back Squeeze', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Back Squeeze is a movement exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '88901201', '88901201-Standing-Back-Squeeze-(VERSION-2)-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.425788+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Back Squeeze. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Standing Back Squeeze', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c514f6f2-3138-489d-8171-69a6063fc30a', 'Front Toe Tap Walks - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Alternate Front Toe Tap Walks is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic stepping movements. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '97771201', '97771201-Alternate-Front-Toe-Tap-Walks-(female)_Plyometrics.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.412523+00', '1. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 2. Set up in the starting position for Alternate Front Toe Tap Walks. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Front Toe Tap Walks - Alternating', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c5157b55-eee7-4d69-b55b-87d6bcf7dfa4', 'Wood Chop (Kettlebell)', 'Core', 'Kettlebell', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build rotational power and define your waistline with the Kettlebell Wood Chop. Secondary activation of your shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '80501201', '80501201-Kettlebell-Wood-Chop-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Wood Chop. 2. Set up in the starting position for Kettlebell Wood Chop. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your obliques. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 58, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'woodchop', 'Wood Chop', 'russian_twist, pallof_press, cable_crunch', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('c520f6a8-8265-46d3-a819-cd74dc5288b5', 'Front Raise (Kettlebell)', 'Shoulders', 'Kettlebell', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your front delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '58591201', '58591201-Kettlebell-Front-Raise_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Front Raise. 2. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('c5324967-e1ef-481a-9398-7d12dda6b507', 'Standing Twist Stretch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Work your side abdominals with this stretching exercise that strengthens your obliques. The standing position engages your core for stability. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '73131201', '73131201-Standing-Twist-Stretch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Twist Stretch. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Standing Twist Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c535d859-0a27-4970-ac2a-7f3c713d5c3d', 'Kickstand Reach Lat Lean', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your lats, the Kickstand Reach Lat Lean helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '85411201', '85411201-Kickstand-Reach-Lat-Lean-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.504261+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Kickstand Reach Lat Lean. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Kickstand Reach Lat Lean', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c53b7e41-79d2-497e-9531-4572bd67bd72', 'Romanian Deadlift (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Romanian Deadlift is a lower body hip hinge exercise that targets your hamstrings/glutes. You''ll also feel your glutes, lower back working to support the movement. The kettlebell''s offset center of mass increases the stability challenge. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '69311201', '69311201-Kettlebell-Romanian-Deadlift-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Romanian Deadlift. 2. Push your hips back, lowering the weight along your legs with a flat back. 3. Lower until you feel a stretch in your hamstrings. 4. Drive hips forward to stand, squeezing glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Romanian Deadlift', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('c54245da-a172-4fc0-add9-375b52dfa7e8', 'String Pull (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Back', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Biceps"}'::text[], 'The String Pull is an arm pulling exercise targeting your upper back. The biceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '65791201', '65791201-String-Pull-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.340041+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for String Pull. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your upper back. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 38, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'String Pull', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('c5442555-9a77-46c6-b572-5e870febedde', 'Standing Hip Thrust (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Core"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this thrusting movement that emphasizes the glutes. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '27441201', '27441201-Cable-Standing-Hip-Thrust-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Hip Thrust. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 4. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 5. Lower your hips back down with control. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_thrust', 'Standing Hip Thrust', 'glute_bridge, romanian_deadlift, leg_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('c5482207-7939-44f9-aa71-98af8c90fd09', 'Wide Bench Press (Barbell)', 'Chest', 'Barbell, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pressing movement that develops pressing power. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '1221201', '01221201-Barbell-Wide-Bench-Press_Chest.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. Load a barbell and set it on a bench rack at the appropriate height. 2. Use a wide grip (wider than shoulder-width) for this variation. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bench_press', 'Wide Bench Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('c552a24e-4177-4ee5-842d-119d4ca17291', 'Moving Child Pose', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your back, the Moving Child Pose helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Secondary activation of your hips provides additional muscle engagement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '81301201', '81301201-Moving-Child-Pose-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.532804+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Moving Child Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Moving Child Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c55e31d0-1bae-472a-ac0e-210797ffc978', 'Air Pillow Crunch (Balance Pad)', 'Core', 'Balance Pad', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Air Pillow Crunch is a core crunching exercise that primarily targets your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '84811201', '84811201-Air-Pillow-Crunch-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 10, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Air Pillow Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c57ec2b3-168b-4cb1-9572-f0bacec13d27', 'Prone Incline Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '24951201', '24951201-Dumbbell-Prone-Incline-Hammer-Curl-(female)_Upper-.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Prone Incline Hammer Curl. 2. Lie face down (prone position) for Dumbbell Prone Incline Hammer Curl. 3. Use a hammer/neutral grip with palms facing each other throughout. 4. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 5. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 6. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 7. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'incline_press', 'Prone Incline Hammer Curl', 'bench_press, shoulder_press, chest_fly', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c59381bb-d968-4c2c-ac3c-1ca4c27610b2', 'Lying Bent Knee Glute Raise - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Lying Bent Knee Alternating Glute Raise is a hip-dominant raising exercise that targets your glutes. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '94461201', '94461201-Lying-Bent-Knee-Alternating-Glute-Raise-(female)_H.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.133808+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Bent Knee Alternating Glute Raise. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Lying Bent Knee Alternating Glute Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Lying Bent Knee Glute Raise - Alternating', 'crunch, plank, russian_twist, hanging_knee_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c59f2d72-fbb5-49dd-af7a-18e4ee7e418f', 'Floor Hyperextension (Resistance Band)', 'Back', 'Resistance Band', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Floor Hyperextension is a extension exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Your hamstrings, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '24231201', '24231201-Resistance-Band-Floor-Hyperextension-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Floor Hyperextension. 2. Position yourself on the floor for Resistance Band Floor Hyperextension. 3. Raise your torso by extending at the lower back/hips. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Floor Hyperextension', 'good_morning, bird_dog, superman', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('c5a60a43-5c21-48dc-bff0-50e289ac0693', 'Lizard Extension To Twist', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your full body, the Lizard Extension To Twist helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '83851201', '83851201-Lizard-Extension-to-Twist-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.855778+00', '1. Extend through the target joint(s) for Lizard Extension To Twist. 2. Move into the stretch position for Lizard Extension To Twist. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Lizard Extension To Twist', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c5b523b9-f84d-4e16-9129-8f0a8b5ae50c', 'Dynamic Chest Stretch', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This stretching exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '4411201', '04411201-Dynamic-Chest-Stretch-(female)_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.298565+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Dynamic Chest Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_stretch', 'Dynamic Chest Stretch', 'stretch_shoulder, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c5b654ef-a692-4b9c-8ab0-8d94f594785f', 'Single Leg Glute Bridge (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this bridging movement focused on hip extension. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '42911201', '42911201-Dumbbell-Single-Leg-Glute-Bridge_Hip.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Single Leg Glute Bridge', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c5b67bd0-0d53-4b48-ac9f-247e8ddcfb25', 'Standing Abdominal Vacuum', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '54451201', '54451201-Standing-Abdominal-Vacuum-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Abdominal Vacuum. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Abdominal Vacuum', 'plank, crunch, leg_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c5bc8ecd-cf2b-4898-9fc3-427238f74b94', 'Sprinter (TRX)', 'Full Body', 'TRX', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Suspender Sprinter is a lower body movement exercise that targets your cardio. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '11401201', '11401201-Suspender-Sprinter-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Sprinter. 2. Set up in the starting position for Suspender Sprinter. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 40, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'sprint', 'Suspender Sprinter', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('c5cea7ca-65e4-45c3-9ace-6a0b35019541', 'Twist Turn Slam', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This dynamic twisting movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '55411201', '55411201-Twist-Turn-Slam_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Twist Turn Slam. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Twist Turn Slam', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c5d3cae0-6586-4ee2-9eb4-0d3f7c87b889', 'Bicep Curl (Kettlebell)', 'Arms', 'Kettlebell', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '58571201', '58571201-Kettlebell-Biceps-Curl_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Biceps Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Biceps Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('c5d59c97-2940-44f4-adb7-d1838406dc24', 'Sit Up (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '107131201', '107131201-Dumbbell-Sit-up-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Sit Up. 2. Set up in the starting position for Dumbbell Sit Up. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c5e77c08-b3e6-476f-87aa-c725638aa788', 'Plyo Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Plyo Push Up is a pushing exercise that targets your chest muscles. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '13061201', '13061201-Plyo-Push-Up_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Plyo Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c60a8646-cef9-4a4a-9ef7-610e05e3d644', 'Crab Twist Toe Touch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'This twisting movement focuses on your obliques for a complete core workout. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '39331201', '39331201-Crab-Twist-Toe-Touch-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Crab Twist Toe Touch. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'toe_touch', 'Crab Twist Toe Touch', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c6254f03-e03c-45fc-a0fb-fde685f8f032', 'Child Pose Back Shift', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your back, the Child Pose Back Shift helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. The hips assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '82331201', '82331201-Child-Pose-Back-Shift-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Child Pose Back Shift. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Child Pose Back Shift', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c62af67a-1548-4db4-abc3-fe2cb402cc79', 'Negative Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this pushing movement targeting your chest. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '71811201', '71811201-Negative-Push-up-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Focus on a slow, controlled lowering phase (3-5 seconds). 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Negative Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c62c88af-ccd6-4627-bd67-299380d8c815', 'Deep Sumo Squat Hold', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement.', '66851201', '66851201-Deep-Sumo-Squat-Hold-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Deep Sumo Squat Hold', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c63578eb-75b9-48e9-88e8-c6e581c12af8', 'Side Wrist Pull Stretch', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build grip strength and forearm size with this pulling exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '43081201', '43081201-Side-Wrist-Pull-Stretch-(female)_Forearms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Side Wrist Pull Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your forearms. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Side Wrist Pull Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c643fc12-876b-4b23-a079-e0c934d490f8', 'Side Step Swipes', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Side Step Swipes is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic stepping movements. Your quads work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '66541201', '66541201-Side-Step-Swipes-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Step Swipes. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Side Step Swipes', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c6556f41-3121-4d1b-9cb1-8c2ff69e5d22', 'Seated 8 Leg Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Seated 8 Leg Crunch, focusing on your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '42601201', '42601201-Seated-8-Leg-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Seated 8 Leg Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c6581693-58f5-4711-8708-58b577793a05', 'Hands Up Knee Up', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Hands Up Knee Up is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '65281201', '65281201-Hands-Up-Knee-Up-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.172397+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Hands Up Knee Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Hands Up Knee Up', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c65b8d0e-31f7-4178-a810-6660f52aa932', 'Standing Reverse Butterfly (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This flying exercise works your chest for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Secondary activation of your front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '92071201', '92071201-Dumbbell-Standing-Reverse-Butterfly-(female)_Shoul.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Reverse Butterfly. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 4. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 5. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'groin_stretch', 'Standing Reverse Butterfly', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, face_pull, bent_over_row', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c66201b9-e87f-4020-a14f-0a5166373e23', 'Seated Cat Cow Pose', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your spine, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Secondary activation of your core provides additional muscle engagement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '61531201', '61531201-Sitting-Cat-Cow-Pose-(female)_Stretching-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.628647+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Cat Cow Pose. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction. A solid choice for stretching day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Seated Cat Cow Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c6666905-5243-40d0-a464-c6fdb97f1a8d', 'Butterfly Yoga Pose Baddha Konasana Variation', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your adductors, the Butterfly Yoga Pose Baddha Konasana Variation helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. You''ll also feel your hips working to support the movement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '97621201', '97621201-Butterfly-Yoga-Pose-Baddha-Konasana-Variation-(fem.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.723232+00', '1. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 2. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 3. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'groin_stretch', 'Butterfly Yoga Pose Baddha Konasana Variation', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c66cd444-c4e0-4f43-a975-9968bb4cd9d9', 'Tuck To Hamstring Stretch (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Tuck To Hamstring Stretch is a flexibility exercise that targets your hamstrings, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. The lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '79101201', '79101201-Tuck-to-Hamstring-Stretch-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Tuck To Hamstring Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 28, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hamstring_stretch', 'Tuck To Hamstring Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_calf, stretch_back', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('c67e9c6a-0672-4634-95f3-d952a7347557', 'Roll Foot', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your full body with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '53981201', '53981201-Roll-Foot_Feet_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Roll Foot. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Roll Foot', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c683901e-b60f-4bb4-8092-369a7bec7965', 'Push Up - Close Grip', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Close Grip Push Up targets your triceps through a pushing motion. Secondary activation of your chest, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '26151201', '26151201-Close-Grip-Push-up-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Push Up - Close Grip', 'Push Up - Close Grip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c690eb66-343c-4ae0-ba56-e2463fc3d8e8', 'Jack Knife Sit Up', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Jack Knife Sit Up is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '38841201', '38841201-Jack-knife-Sit-up-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Jack Knife Sit Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Jack Knife Sit Up', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c69606b6-ad57-4533-86c5-144a438d965c', 'Squat Knees Middle Position (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '66251201', '66251201-Barbell-Squat---Knees---Middle position-(WRONG-RIGHT)-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Set up a barbell in a rack at the appropriate height for Barbell Squat Knees Middle Position. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Squat Knees Middle Position', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('c6a632ca-c9b5-471c-bb10-2fa9ead47be5', 'Double High Knee Side Hop', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Calves"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '76421201', '76421201-Double-High-Knee-Side-Hop-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Double High Knee Side Hop. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'high_knees', 'Double High Knee Side Hop', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c6ce4a6d-f672-4d7d-b02e-92e73a931398', 'Decline Chest Press - Single Arm (Machine)', 'Chest', 'Machine', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The decline position targets the lower portion of the muscles more intensely. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '88081201', '88081201-Lever-Decline-Single-Arm-Chest-Press_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.242428+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Decline Single Arm Chest Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Press', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Unilateral', NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 76, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Lever Decline Single Arm Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('c6dbb0b8-168c-4d36-9964-c6518f7d0177', 'Crunch (Stability Ball)', 'Core', 'Stability Ball', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this crunching movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. The stability ball adds an instability challenge that activates more stabilizer muscles. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '27011201', '27011201-Crunch-(on-stability-ball)-(female)_waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Crunch. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'stability_ball', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c6dfe969-25ed-4174-92e6-166a058d1faf', 'Battling Ropes Waves With Kneeling Get - Alternating', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Core"}'::text[], 'Build total body strength and coordination with this multi-joint movement movement. Secondary activation of your shoulders, core provides additional muscle engagement. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Compound movements like this develop coordination, power, and overall fitness.', '41311201', '41311201-Battling-Ropes-Alternating-Waves-with-Kneeling-Get.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Battling Ropes Waves With Kneeling Get - Alternating', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c6e4311d-5060-4116-aa13-3ffdde4a5d0a', 'Bench Dip (Stability Ball)', 'Chest', 'Stability Ball, Flat Bench', '{"Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Bench Dip On Stability Ball targets your triceps through a dipping motion. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. Using a ball requires constant core engagement to maintain balance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '55131201', '55131201-Bench-Dip-on-Stability-Ball_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.422129+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Bench Dip On Stability Ball. 2. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 3. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Bench Dip On Stability Ball', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c7331c59-2e1b-4959-96e1-77efe488bb14', 'Seated Hip Adduction (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Hip Adduction Machine', '{"Inner Thighs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Lever Seated Hip Adduction is a lower body movement exercise that targets your adductors. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '36121201', '36121201-Lever-Seated-Hip-Adduction-(female)_Thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.855778+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Hip Adduction. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_adduction', 'Lever Seated Hip Adduction', 'hip_abduction, squat, lunge', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('c73f8388-e0d9-47ab-95b9-402dc0c44e3e', 'Ab Coaster Oblique Crunch (Machine)', 'Core', 'Ab Machine', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '79811201', '79811201-Lever-Ab-Coaster-Oblique-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Ab Coaster Oblique Crunch. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Lever Ab Coaster Oblique Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('c743346c-3ce8-4f12-a8b7-a1a75591d919', 'Front Plank Arm Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Front Plank Arm Raise is a core raising exercise that primarily targets your abs. Secondary activation of your shoulders, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '46221201', '46221201-Dumbbell-Front-Plank-Arm-Raise_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Front Plank Arm Raise. 2. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Front Plank Arm Raise', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'dumbbell', TRUE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c749dbdc-68e7-49fa-b7be-be01d63c1007', 'Forward Side Top Press', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements. This variation is excellent for building mind-muscle connection.', '78201201', '78201201-Forward-Side-Top-Presses-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 2. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 3. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Forward Side Top Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c74b5528-7354-45ea-8d12-cd9d8df413a6', 'Mountain Climber', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Mountain Climber builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Your hip flexors, shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '52131201', '52131201-Mountain-Climber-(VERSION-2)-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.532804+00', '1. From plank position, drive one knee toward your chest. 2. Quickly switch legs, bringing the other knee forward. 3. Continue alternating at a quick pace while maintaining plank form. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'mountain_climber', 'Mountain Climber', 'burpee, plank, high_knees', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c7526bc9-defe-4833-893b-23232ca17c19', 'Seated Military Press In Out Leg Raise On Floor (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Seated Military Press In Out Leg Raise On Floor is a core pressing exercise that primarily targets your abs. Your triceps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '68011201', '68011201-Dumbbell-Seated-Military-Press-In-Out-Leg-Raise-on-Floor_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Seated Military Press In Out Leg Raise On Floor. 2. Position yourself on the floor for Dumbbell Seated Military Press In Out Leg Raise On Floor. 3. Sit on the floor with your legs positioned as required. 4. Execute the pressing motion for Dumbbell Seated Military Press In Out Leg Raise On Floor, extending through the target muscles. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 89, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'shoulder_press', 'Seated Military Press In Out Leg Raise On Floor', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('c7532e16-04d8-43df-ac31-30923ea2caf5', 'Lying Svend Press', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '90461201', '90461201-Bodyweight-Lying-Svend-Press-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Bodyweight Lying Svend Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squeeze_press', 'Lying Svend Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c7593ca9-0677-455b-b8d3-7941d551caa5', 'Diagonal Front Scoop Raise', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Diagonal Front Scoop Raise is a raising exercise that targets your chest muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '63061201', '63061201-Diagonal-Front-Scoop-Raise(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Diagonal Front Scoop Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c766b616-378e-4319-a988-cee723cc06bb', 'T Twist Knee Drive', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity twisting exercise that challenges your entire body. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '54611201', '54611201-T-Twist-Knee-Drive-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for T Twist Knee Drive. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'T Twist Knee Drive', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c7712407-2905-42df-9c7c-09bc8b7ee0f6', 'Heel Together Slight Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '88651201', '88651201-Heel-Together-Slight-Squat-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. Great for building strength in your quads.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Heel Together Slight Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c77925d4-edfc-44a6-acae-234c60e66d4e', 'Donkey Calf Raise', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build stronger calves with this targeted raising exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '26771201', '26771201-Donkey-Calf-Raise-(female)_Calves.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 2. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 3. Lower with control and repeat. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Donkey Calf Raise', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c7816d88-4313-4450-a3ba-5f9e7f7577fb', 'Hip Extension (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Lever Machine', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This extension exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '96881201', '96881201-Lever-Hip-Extension-(VERSION-2)-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.724336+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Hip Extension. 2. Extend through the target joint(s) for Lever Hip Extension. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Lever Hip Extension', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('c784b564-bcb6-469f-bbd9-200d3c7298a8', 'Standing Lateral Stretch', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Standing Lateral Stretch provides a deep stretch for your lats, ideal for recovery and mobility work. The standing position engages your core for stability. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '7941201', '07941201-Standing-Lateral-Stretch_Back-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.452942+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Move into the stretch position for Standing Lateral Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Standing Lateral Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c78828b7-36d5-403a-a080-6c0b5bb0412d', 'Bent Over Overhead Triceps Extension Straight (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Cable Bent Over Overhead Triceps Extension Straig targets your triceps through a extension motion. Bending over allows gravity to provide resistance in a different plane. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '107651201', '107651201-Cable-Bent-Over-Overhead-Triceps-Extension-Straig.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.71819+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Bent Over Overhead Triceps Extension Straig. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 4. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Bent Over Overhead Triceps Extension Straight', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('c78947a3-2d9e-44a3-83e7-24ce32ae7861', 'Decline Chest Press (Chair)', 'Chest', 'Chair', '{"Chest","Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Seated Decline Chest Press On A Chair, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '86201201', '86201201-Seated-Decline-Chest-Press-on-a-Chair-(male)_Chest.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', 'Press', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'decline_press', 'Seated Decline Chest Press On A Chair', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, chest_fly, dip', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c78e639a-a927-4339-896d-73faa6fff1e2', 'Standing Isometric Shoulder External Rotation Wit', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This rotation exercise works your rotator cuff for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '101261201', '101261201-Standing-Isometric-Shoulder-External-Rotation-wit.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.7451+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Isometric Shoulder External Rotation Wit. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 47, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'external_rotation', 'Standing Isometric Shoulder External Rotation Wit', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c7aae7b5-1ec6-41ab-be5d-0eba72bf58af', 'Kneeling Plank Arm Raise - Alternating', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this raising movement that works your abs. The shoulders, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '104511201', '104511201-Kneeling-Plank-Alternating-Arm-Raise_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.271124+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Kneeling Plank Alternating Arm Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Kneeling Plank Arm Raise - Alternating', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c7b2d00f-d7ee-477a-8a69-c19c9a5887d0', 'Superman Hold', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your lower back. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '68861201', '68861201-Superman-Hold-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.991486+00', '1. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. 2. Set up in the starting position for Superman Hold. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your lower back. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Superman Hold', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('c7b6ce35-92ba-40b7-9590-6c006f320014', 'Curtsy Lunge Slide (Towel)', 'Legs', 'Towel', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this lunging exercise for quad development. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '80981201', '80981201-Curtsy-Lunge-Slide-with-Towel-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. A solid choice for legs day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Curtsy Lunge Slide With Towel', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65);
